RF.put("questb:b42",{"8602":{"id":8602,"t":"Stormcaller's Pauldrons","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 9,950, 0.66 times as much.","obj":"Bring the Qiraji Bindings of Dominance, 2 Idols of Life, 5 Gold Scarabs and 5 Crystal Scarabs to Andorgos in Ahn'Qiraj. You must also attain Neutral reputation with the Brood of Nozdormu to complete this quest.\nQiraji Bindings of Dominance Viscidus in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Princess Huhuran in Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n2 Idol of Life Vekniss Soldier 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Stinger 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Gold Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Crystal Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 0 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","desc":"It is said among us that the ornate shoulder armor worn by the mortal races started as an attempt to emulate the wings of a dragon.\nBring me the bindings worn by the highest Qiraji leaders and I shall shape them into a set of pauldrons more dreadful than even the wings of Nefarian himself!","rew":"You will receive:\nStormcaller's Pauldrons\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"Have you collected the components I require?","done":"From the materials you bring and from the scales of our fallen Qiraji foes I make you these pauldrons, mortal. May they grant you the protection you need and may the sight of them strike fear into our enemies.\nStart Andorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Andorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Horde Class Shaman Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8602\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 13,200 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Stormcaller's Pauldrons this quest\nBring the Qiraji Bindings of Dominance, 2 Idols of Life, 5 Gold Scarabs and 5 Crystal Scarabs to Andorgos in Ahn'Qiraj.\nAndorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8522":{"id":8522,"t":"The Alliance Needs Runecloth Bandages!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 1 instead of 56.","obj":"Bring 20 Runecloth Bandages to Keeper Moonshade at the Military Ward in Ironforge.\n20 Runecloth Bandage","desc":"Argue the merits of the war if you will, ‹class›, but it has already been set in motion. Look around you at your family and friends, and then ask yourself what it is that you can do to see to it that if they are involved, they will have every advantage to survive the conflagration.\nTo that end, I am collecting runecloth bandages here from whatever source. Would you like to make a donation?","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Alliance Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","back":"The days pass one after the other, and still we go on. ‹class›, have you those runecloth bandages?","done":"You are to be commended, ‹class›, for your perseverance in this task. I shall put these bandages away, and then I should like to talk to you again about the possibility of your collecting even more runecloth bandages.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":59.8,"y":33.6,"n":"Keeper Moonshade","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"522":{"id":522,"t":"Assassin's Contract","lv":38,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Assassin's Contract to Magistrate Maleb in Southshore.\nAssassin's Contract Shadowy Assassin\nProvided: Assassin's Contract","desc":"This is a contract for the assassination of Magistrate Henry Maleb. It was sealed and stamped in red wax, using a distinctive signet ring.","rew":"Experience: 700\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","back":"You look out of breath! Do you have something to report?","done":"<Maleb inspects the contract.>\nThat explains the latest attack on Southshore. The Syndicate must be after me, just as they were the last magistrate!","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":48.1,"y":59.1,"n":"Magistrate Henry Maleb","e":1}],"cats":["alterac-mountains"]},"7162":{"id":7162,"t":"Proving Grounds","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to the Icewing Caverns located southwest of Dun Baldar in Alterac Valley and recover the Stormpike Banner. Return the Stormpike Banner to Lieutenant Haggerdin in the Alterac Mountains.\nStormpike Banner Stormpike Banner in Alterac Valley","desc":"You've arrived just in time, ‹class›. These Frostwolf savages just won't give up! We must show them the might of the Stormpike. They must bow to our superiority.\nBefore you make your way to the field of battle, you will want to join the rank of Stormpike.\nSouthwest of Dun Baldar, you will find the Icewing Caverns. Planted deep within the caverns is a Stormpike Banner. Venture forth and recover that banner. Return it to me, and you will have earned a Stormpike initiate's insignia.","rew":"You will receive:\nStormpike Insignia Rank 1 The Frostwolf Artichoke\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Stormpike Guard\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Beware the harpies of the region, ‹class›. They'll not think twice to rip out your throat!","done":"Take and wear this insignia with pride, ‹name›. As your rank among the Stormpike grows, so too will the insignia. Return to me as you gain honor with Stormpike, and I shall replace your insignia with other, more powerful insignias.\nPerhaps someday you will grow to be a legend on this field of battle. Should that day ever come, you will be granted the Eye of Command.","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":39.5,"y":81.2,"n":"Lieutenant Haggerdin","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["alterac-valley"]},"7002":{"id":7002,"t":"Ram Hide Harnesses","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"null\nAlterac Ram Hide Alterac Ram 79.7 % in Alterac Valley , Stabled Alterac Ram 79.7 % in Alterac Valley","desc":"While some of our soldiers are busy capturing wolves for the stable master, others must provide for the simple necessities that riding requires. I am speaking of riding harnesses, of course.\nYou must strike at the indigenous rams of the region. The very same rams that the Stormpike cavalry uses as mounts!\nSlay them and return to me with their hides. Once we have gathered enough hides, we will fashion harnesses for the riders. The Frostwolf Wolf Riders will ride once more!","back":"Slay them and return to me with their hides. The same rams that the Stormpike cavalry uses as mounts!","done":"Well done, soldier. I will notify you when I have stockpiled enough of the hides.\nCarry on!\nStart Frostwolf Wolf Rider Commander Alterac Valley End Frostwolf Wolf Rider Commander Alterac Valley Level 60 , requires level 51 Difficulty 51 56 58 Side Horde Type PvP Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 7002","cats":["alterac-valley"]},"7082":{"id":7082,"t":"The Graveyards of Alterac","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays 90s instead of 0.","obj":"Assault a graveyard, then return to Corporal Teeka Bloodsnarl in the Alterac Mountains.\nGraveyard Assaulted","desc":"The battle lines of Alterac Valley are ever shifting. Territories swing back and forth as we meet our opponents in deadly combat. And graveyards, ‹name›, are where battles rage most fierce.\nI want you to attack an Alliance held graveyard! Find a graveyard with an Alliance banner in its midst and pull it from the ground.\nDo that and your task for me will be complete, but... if you hold the graveyard for a few minutes, then it will be ours and troops will come and relieve you.","rew":"Money: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Frostwolf Clan\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Attack a graveyard held by the Alliance!","done":"Well done, ‹name›! With each graveyard under our control, the spirits of our enemies will wander more lost and aimless.","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":65.6,"y":55.1,"n":"Corporal Teeka Bloodsnarl","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["alterac-valley"]},"7402":{"id":7402,"t":"Wanted: ORCS!","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"You have been tasked with slaying opposing Orc players in Alterac Valley.\nKill an Orc and take their Orc Tooth back to Corporal Noreg Stormpike at Dun Baldar.\nOrc Tooth Alliance Sentinel , Stormpike Mountaineer , Winterax Berserker , Frostwolf in Alterac Valley and 4 more","desc":"By order of Corporal Noreg Stormpike, all able bodied soldiers of Stormpike are required to slay any opposing orcs that they meet upon the field of battle.\nSoldiers are required to remove a tusk or tooth from the maw of the enemy and present said tooth as proof of their accomplishment.\nWear protective gloves.","rew":"Money: 1 80 1 gold, 80 silver, 0 copper Experience: 9,550\nStart Wanted: ORCS! Level 60 , requires level 51 Difficulty 51 56 58 Side Both factions Type PvP Shareable Yes Quest ID 7402","cats":["alterac-valley"]},"8442":{"id":8442,"t":"Conquering Arathi Basin","lv":59,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Arathi Basin Mark of Honor to a Horde Warbringer outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Arathi Basin Mark of Honor","desc":"Our conflict with the Alliance has escalated to a true war. No longer are false pretenses to enter into battle used or expected by either side at this point.\nThe battle for the Arathi Basin is one of resources, plain and simple. Either the Alliance gets the resources and uses them against us or we get them and use them to keep our war efforts going. Help the Defilers maintain the flow of resources we need, ‹name›!","rew":"Experience: 3,200\n+50 reputation with The Defilers","back":"You've come back with news from Arathi, ‹class›?","done":"Securing our resources in Arathi is an important task! You've done well, ‹name›.\nThe Barrens Arathi Highlands Undercity","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":46.7,"y":8.7,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.5,"y":29.1,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":58.3,"y":97.9,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-basin"]},"8122":{"id":8122,"t":"Take Five Bases","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Hold five bases in Arathi Basin at the same time, then return to Deathmaster Dwire in Hammerfall.","desc":"It is difficult to see, so deep we are in the conflict, but our spies report a weakening in the League of Arathor's resolve. We must use this window and strike a brutal blow against them! Return to Arathi Basin and throw yourself against our foes. Curse them and kill them and control all five strategic bases! Send their soldiers screaming and bleeding from the front lines, with stories of your cruelty on their mewling lips.\nDo this, and score a great victory for the Defilers.","rew":"You will receive:\nBattle Tabard of the Defilers\nMoney: 2 70 2 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with The Defilers","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.3,"y":29.7,"n":"Deathmaster Dwire","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-basin"]},"682":{"id":682,"t":"Stromgarde Badges","lv":37,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Stromgarde Librarian Leggings, Stromgarde Operative Pants.","obj":"Bring 7 Stromgarde Badges to Captain Nials at Refuge Pointe.\n7 Stromgarde Badge Syndicate Magus 80 % , Syndicate Conjuror 80 % , Syndicate Prowler 80 %","desc":"The Syndicate in Stromgarde do battle with our contingent of militia there. In order to urge the rabble to fight our more disciplined troops, the Syndicate leaders have placed a bounty on our soldiers, awarding gold for each Stromgarde Badge gathered off killed militiamen.\nWe want those badges retrieved - we cannot allow the cutthroats to take trophies from our brave fallen!\nEnter the Syndicate-controlled area of Stromgarde and hunt them for our badges.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nStromgarde Cavalry Leggings Stromgarde Librarian Leggings Stromgarde Operative Pants\nNew in Forever: Stromgarde Librarian Leggings, Stromgarde Operative Pants.\nYou will also receive:\nStromgarde Cavalry Leggings\nExperience: 3,550\n+150 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Have you retrieved any Stromgarde Badges, ‹name›? The Syndicate must learn they cannot profit from our dead.","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. We will inform the families of these fallen soldiers that they were killed in battle.\nIt will be grim news to bear, but it is better than the uncertainty of a missing loved one.","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":45.8,"y":47.6,"n":"Captain Nials","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"6442":{"id":6442,"t":"Naga at the Zoram Strand","lv":19,"min":14,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 20 Wrathtail Heads to Marukai along the Zoram Strand.\n20 Wrathtail Head Wrathtail Priestess , Wrathtail Sorceress , Wrathtail Sea Witch , Wrathtail Wave Rider and 2 more","desc":"There is evil lurking here along the coast, ‹race›.\nIt is the resting place of the doomed city of Zoram, long destroyed and submerged beneath the seas. Lost, and nearly forgotten.\nNow, the naga have returned, and for what reason we do not know. But reason matters little; we must defend the land we have worked so hard to claim as our own.\nReturn to me with 20 of their heads! Throw the naga back to the depths!","rew":"Experience: 1,450\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"The naga increase in numbers, ‹name›. Please complete this task for me.","done":"We could use more of your kind around here, ‹name›. Thank you for your help.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":11.7,"y":34.9,"n":"Marukai","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"6922":{"id":6922,"t":"Baron Aquanis","lv":30,"min":21,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 7,250 experience instead of 3,050, 2.38 times as much. New rewards: Dreamer's Chestguard. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved what dungeon quests give beyond a normal quest.","obj":"Bring the Strange Water Globe to Je'neu Sancrea at Zoram'gar Outpost, Ashenvale.\nStrange Water Globe Baron Aquanis\nProvided: Strange Water Globe","desc":"The defeated water elemental has left behind a strange water globe. You surmise that the object somehow fed the beast energy. Inside the globe, a putrid-looking form of water sloshes about. The globe itself seems impervious to any sort of physical force.\nIf anyone can make any sense of this item, it would be Je'neu Sancrea of the Earthen Ring. He is located at the Horde's Zoram'gar Outpost in Ashenvale.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nOutlaw Sabre Witch's Finger Dreamer's Chestguard\nNew in Forever: Dreamer's Chestguard.\nExperience: 7,250\n+150 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Ah, hello again ‹name›. I was just reading the waves the sea, much like I always do. What brings you to the outpost?","done":"This... this is quite the find, ‹name›.\nYou acquired this from Baron Aquanis in Blackfathom, you say? Baron Aquanis has long been thought of as a corrupted elemental power; this globe will prove what exactly had corrupted him. While it would be no surprise if it turned out to be the Twilight's Hammer, our studies will also show how they did it as well.\nYou did well in bringing this to me. Please - take this, along with the Earthen Ring's warmest regards.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":11.6,"y":34.3,"n":"Je'neu Sancrea","e":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"3562":{"id":3562,"t":"Magatha's Payment to Jediga","lv":52,"min":45,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver Magatha's Note to Jediga in Azshara.\nMagatha's Note\nProvided: Magatha's Note","desc":"Take this note to Jediga. Tell her the payment will be here for her when she returns. And tell her I am pleased with her work.\nGo swiftly, ‹name›. Tell your master I will be awaiting her here.","rew":"Money: 60 0 gold, 60 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,800","back":"Well, what did Magatha say? The old crone... I bet she was less than polite.","done":"Ah, good. She was much more reasonable than I expected... at least towards you. I half expected her to have you punished for my insolence in sending someone in my place. She must really want that tablet. Interesting.\nSomething to ponder another time.\nThunder Bluff Azshara","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":69.9,"y":30.9,"n":"Magatha Grimtotem","s":1},{"z":"Azshara","x":22.6,"y":51.4,"n":"Jediga","e":1}],"cats":["azshara"]},"762":{"id":762,"t":"An Ambassador of Evil","lv":44,"min":35,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill Ambassador Infernus in Angor Fortress and bring proof of his death to Advisor Belgrum in Ironforge.\nAmbassador Infernus' Bracer Ambassador Infernus","desc":"Ambassador Infernus was sent to Angor Fortress by Ragnaros himself to mind the Shadowforge seeking lost artifacts in Uldaman.\nIt has already meant tremendous casualties for our people, but it has obviously grown worse. I hesitate to guess how many artifacts they would be able to find and use against Ironforge.\nOur goal is simple, ‹class›. Return to the Badlands and destroy Ambassador Infernus. Once the threat is eliminated, return to Advisor Belgrum with proof of your victory.\nIt is in your hands now.","rew":"You will receive:\nDwarf Captain's Sword\nMoney: 1 25 1 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,650\n+150 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Time is of the essence, ‹name›. Ragnaros will not wait for us to prepare.","done":"‹name›, your dedication to Ironforge and to the dwarven people cannot be refuted. I thank you for your help in this matter.\nI shall send word to Historian Karnik informing him that you have succeeded, and I shall also have aid sent to the Badlands as soon as possible to help recover the excavation site. Thank you again.\nBefore you go, there is one more thing I would ask of you in the name of King Bronzebeard.\nDun Morogh Badlands","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":63.5,"y":23,"n":"Historian Karnik","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":63.5,"y":22.6,"n":"Advisor Belgrum","e":1}],"cats":["badlands"]},"3802":{"id":3802,"t":"Dark Iron Legacy","lv":52,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Slay Fineous Darkvire and recover the great hammer, Ironfel. Take Ironfel to the Shrine of Thaurissan and place it on the statue of Franclorn Forgewright.\nIronfel Fineous Darkvire","desc":"You will find Fineous Darkvire beyond the Ring of Law, in the Hall of Crafting. Kill the miserable cur and recover Ironfel.\nTake Ironfel to the Shrine of Thaurissan and place the hammer in its rightful place: In the hands of the statue erected in my honor.\nWhen this is done, the compartment in which I stored the master key will open. More importantly, Ironfel will remain forever in my grasp. Should they make an attempt to remove the hammer; both the statue and hammer will shatter, lost forever.","rew":"You will receive:\nShadowforge Key\nMoney: 2 30 2 gold, 30 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,100","back":"The statue looms ominously above you.","done":"The hammer slides firmly into place, within the grasp of the massive Dark Iron monument. A tiny compartment opens at the base of the statue. Inside you find...\nBurning Steppes Searing Gorge","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":29,"y":28.9,"n":"Franclorn Forgewright","s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-depths"]},"4282":{"id":4282,"t":"A Shred of Hope","lv":58,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return Marshal Windsor's Lost Information.\nMarshal Windsor believes that the information is being held by Golem Lord Argelmach and General Angerforge.\nMarshal Windsor's Lost Information General Angerforge\nMarshal Windsor's Lost Information Golem Lord Argelmach","desc":"<Marshal Windsor shakes the note excitedly.>\nDo you realize what this means, ‹name›?\nPerhaps all is not lost! From what I can ascertain, the information is being held by two Dark Iron dwarves: General Angerforge and the golem lord, Argelmach. I have a feeling that they won't just hand over the information if we ask nicely.\nI hope you are ready to battle.\nVenture forth and find these two villains! Destroy them and return my lost information.","rew":"Money: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,200\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Soon this grand subterfuge will be over.","done":"<Marshal Windsor snatches the two tablets from your hands.>\nWe need to get out of here!\nStart Marshal Windsor End Marshal Windsor Level 58 , requires level 50 Difficulty 50 54 56 Side Alliance Type Dungeon Shareable Yes Quest ID 4282\nThe chain\n16 quests from level 54 to 60, 77,300 XP in all.\n1 [ 54 ] Dragonkin Menace\nSlay 15 Black Broodlings, 10 Black Dragonspawn, 4 Black Wyrmkin and 1 Black Drake.\nHelendis Riverhorn Burning Steppes\n5,450 XP\n2 [ 54 ] The True Masters\nTravel to Lakeshire and deliver Helendis Riverhorn's Letter to Magistrate Solomon.\nHelendis Riverhorn Burning Steppes\n4,100 XP\n3 [ 54 ] The True Masters\nTravel to Stormwind and deliver Solomon's Plea to Highlord Bolvar Fordragon. Bolvar resides in Stormwind Keep.\nMagistrate Solomon Redridge Mountains\n4,100 XP\n4 [ 54 ] The True Masters\nSpeak with Highlord Bolvar Fordragon after speaking with Lady Katrana Prestor.\nHighlord Bolvar Fordragon Stormwind City\n550 XP\n5 [ 54 ] The True Masters\nTake Bolvar's Decree to Magistrate Solomon in Lakeshire.\nHighlord Bolvar Fordragon Stormwind City\n5,450 XP\n6 [ 54 ] The True Masters\nSpeak with Marshal Maxwell in the Burning Steppes.\nMagistrate Solomon Redridge Mountains\n550 XP\n7 [ 54 ] The True Masters\nSpeak with Ragged John to learn of Marshal Windsor's fate and return to Marshal Maxwell when you have completed this task. You recall Marshal Maxwell telling you to search for h\nMarshal Maxwell Burning Steppes\n550 XP\n8 [ 54 ] Marshal Windsor\nTravel to Blackrock Mountain in the northwest and enter Blackrock Depths.\nMarshal Maxwell Burning Steppes\n5,450 XP\n9 [ 54 ] Abandoned Hope\nGive Marshal Maxwell the bad news.\nMarshal Windsor\n5,450 XP\n10 [ 58 ] A Crumpled Up Note\nYou may have just stumbled on to something that Marshal Windsor would be interested in seeing.\nA Crumpled Up Note\n6,200 XP\n11 [ 58 ] A Shred of Hope this quest\nReturn Marshal Windsor's Lost Information. Marshal Windsor believes that the information is being held by Golem Lord Argelmach and General Angerforge.\nMarshal Windsor\n6,200 XP\n12 [ 58 ] Jail Break!\nHelp Marshal Windsor get his gear back and free his friends.\nMarshal Windsor\n7,750 XP\n13 [ 60 ] Stormwind Rendezvous\nTravel to Stormwind City and venture t","cats":["blackrock-depths"]},"4122":{"id":4122,"t":"Grark Lorkrub","lv":58,"min":52,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to the Burning Steppes and find Grark Lorkrub. You recall Lexlort mentioning that he was last seen in a massive Blackrock fortress.\nWhen you find Grark Lorkrub, use the Thorium Shackles to bind him and then lead him back through Blackrock Mountain to the Searing Gorge. Lexlort will have his men waiting on the other side to take Grark into custody.\nProvided: Thorium Shackles","desc":"I tracked him across the Searing Gorge, through the mountain, and into the Burning Steppes. That traitor was caught red-handed giving the Blackrock orcs vital information about our day to day operations. I'm speaking of Grark Lorkrub.\nHe now sits in the Burning Steppes, safely under their protection - or so he thinks.\nTake these shackles, ‹name›. Find Grark, place the shackles on him and lead him through Blackrock Mountain. Do this and a tribute is yours.","rew":"Experience: 6,200","done":"Can you not see the power we gain by joining the legion of Blackrock?\nBadlands Burning Steppes","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":5.9,"y":47.6,"n":"Lexlort","s":1},{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":40.2,"y":34.2,"n":"Grark Lorkrub","e":1}],"cats":["blackrock-depths"]},"4362":{"id":4362,"t":"The Fate of the Kingdom","lv":59,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Blackrock Depths and rescue Princess Moira Bronzebeard from the evil clutches of Emperor Dagran Thaurissan.\nEmperor Dagran Thaurissan slain","desc":"It would seem as if my old adversary, Dagran Thaurissan, has me and the kingdom of Ironforge at his mercy.\nYou may be my last hope, ‹name›. You must rescue my dear daughter, Moira!\nThere is only one way to make sure that the spell Thaurissan has cast on Moira is broken: Kill him.\nAnd ‹name›, do not harm her! Remember, she is being controlled by Thaurissan! The things she may do or say are a result of Thaurissan's evil spell!","rew":"Experience: 8,050\n+150 reputation with Ironforge","done":"<Princess Bronzebeard weeps over the loss of Emperor Dagran Thaurissan.>\nWhy???","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":57.4,"y":30.1,"n":"King Magni Bronzebeard","s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-depths"]},"5002":{"id":5002,"t":"Message to Maxwell","lv":59,"min":55,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to the Burning Steppes and give Bijou's Information to Marshal Maxwell.\nBijou's Information\nProvided: Bijou's Information","desc":"I'm a goblin of my word, ‹race›. Now listen closely:\nThese orcs are used primarily as beasts of burden and cannon fodder for the black dragonflight!\nTheir true leader is none other than Nefarian, brood of Deathwing. I've also discovered the location of Nefarian's subordinates in this part of the citadel.\nTake this map to Marshal Maxwell in the Burning Steppes. It has the location of these fiends marked for easy identification.","rew":"Money: 1 80 1 gold, 80 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,400\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Ah, ‹name›. It has been a long time.","done":"This coincides with much of what we already knew. Regardless, it is interesting and rather unfortunate information.\nThe markings on this map will prove valuable in thinning the Blackrock menace.","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":84.7,"y":69,"n":"Marshal Maxwell","e":1}],"cats":["blackrock-spire"]},"6602":{"id":6602,"t":"Blood of the Black Dragon Champion","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Blackrock Spire and slay General Drakkisath. Gather his blood and return it to Rexxar.\nBlood of the Black Dragon Champion General Drakkisath","desc":"How would you feel about paying a visit to the General? No illusions, this time.\nCeremony? A pretty word to describe the bloodletting that amuses the Black Dragonflight.\nAll this amulet requires is the blood of General Drakkisath. Primitive security. There are other ways to receive the General's blood.\nGo to Blackrock Spire and kill Drakkisath. Return with his blood and I will activate the key to Onyxia's lair.","rew":"You will receive:\nDrakefire Amulet\nExperience: 9,950","back":"I don't think I need to tell you that Drakkisath is not to be taken lightly.\nI let the thousands dead by his hand do the talking.","done":"A victory that will be remembered for many years, ‹name›. The Drakefire Amulet will open Onyxia's lair. Gather your allies and bring victory to the Horde.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":46.4,"y":18.2,"n":"Rexxar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-spire"]},"2762":{"id":2762,"t":"The Great Silver Deceiver","lv":45,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring forty Mithril Bars and five Truesilver Bars to Galvan the Ancient in Stranglethorn.\n40 Mithril Bar\n5 Truesilver Bar Felsteel Chest 8.6 % , Heavy Fel Iron Chest 5.1 % , Adamantite Bound Chest 5.1 % , Solid Chest 0 % and 4 more","desc":"It is said that truesilver is stronger and more durable than mithril. Galvan does not disagree with this assessment of the minerals, but contrary to its name, truesilver is not true! Mithril is a far nobler mineral! HAH! Regardless, for this lesson you will need to find the great silver deceiver, ‹name›.\nBring me forty bars of mithril and five bars of truesilver. In exchange, you will be taught the secret of ornate mithril gloves and more importantly, learn that truesilver is a liar!","rew":"You will receive:\nPlans: Ornate Mithril Gloves\nExperience: 3,900","back":"After such mining, your muscles bulge and your body aches!","done":"She's a cruel mistress, is she not, ‹name›? I'm speaking of truesilver, naturally. Aye, Galvan spent over a decade in the mountains of Alterac learning this lesson. Take this and learn from it all that you can!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":50.6,"y":20.5,"n":"Galvan the Ancient","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blacksmithing"]},"2602":{"id":2602,"t":"Infallible Mind","lv":50,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring ten Basilisk Brains and two Vulture Gizzards to Bloodmage Lynnore.\n10 Basilisk Brain Redstone Basilisk 40 % , Redstone Crystalhide 40 % , Deatheye 30 %\n2 Vulture Gizzard Black Slayer 40 % , Spiteflayer 30 %","desc":"Your focused concentration has dwindled so soon? More research must be done!\nOh yes, the price remains the same, ‹name›. Venture forth into the blasted lands and return to me with ten brains from the redstone and two vulture gizzards.","rew":"You will receive:\nCerebral Cortex Compound","back":"Have you returned with the requested organs?","done":"Yes, yes, give me a moment and more of the compound will be ready for your consumption, ‹name›.\nTake it... and ‹name›, do not attempt to consume these experimental concoctions in rapid succession. The results could be disastrous.","pins":[{"z":"Blasted Lands","x":50.6,"y":14.3,"n":"Bloodmage Lynnore","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blasted-lands"]},"2522":{"id":2522,"t":"Kum'isha's Endeavors","lv":55,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find and return a Flawless Draenethyst Sphere to Kum'isha the Collector.\nFlawless Draenethyst Sphere Teremus the Devourer , Bonepicker 0 % , Felcular 0 % , Ilifar 0 % and 4 more","desc":"Even though the portal conjuration was a failure, I remain hopeful that my next attempt will be successful.\nThe hope of the Draenei is as fervent as your greed for trinkets, ‹race›. Go back out into these cursed lands and recover another flawless draenethyst sphere.\nOf course, the choice to take on this task is completely left to you *grin*.","rew":"You will receive:\nEmerald Encrusted Chest\nExperience: 5,650","back":"Have you found another flawless draenethyst sphere?","done":"Simply amazing. I had doubted that you could find another sphere, yet here it is, pulsating in my hands.\nWell done, ‹name›!\nShould you find anymore--and I believe this to be an impossibility--return them to me and I shall reward you again.","pins":[{"z":"Blasted Lands","x":52,"y":35.6,"n":"Kum'isha the Collector","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blasted-lands"]},"94282":{"id":94282,"t":"Craftsmans writ craftsmans monocle","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Craftsman's Monocle\nCraftsman's Monocle","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Craftsman's Monocle, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Craftsman's Monocle Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94282","cats":["crafting"]},"7882":{"id":7882,"t":"Carnival Jerkins","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"3 Toughened Leather Armor","rew":"You will receive:\n4 Darkmoon Faire Prize Ticket\n+100 reputation with Darkmoon Faire","back":"Our Faire workers do more than sweep trash and hammer spikes! They also help guard the carnival as it travels, and to that end they are always needing good sturdy armor jerkins.\nIf you make some tough leather armor and bring it to me, then I'll make sure it gets to the right people. I'll also get you some Darkmoon Faire tickets as trade.","done":"Ah, you brought the jerkins. Splendid. What animal's skin did you use to make these, may I ask? The stitch-work is very well done, and the texture of the leather has a rugged style to it. I can tell you are a craftsman of skill!\nThank you, ‹name›, and here are your tickets.\nElwynn Forest Mulgore","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":43.6,"y":70.8,"n":"Chronos","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":37.2,"y":42.5,"n":"Chronos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkmoon-faire"]},"1002":{"id":1002,"t":"Buzzbox 323","lv":14,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect 6 Moonstalker Fangs and place them in Buzzbox 323.\n6 Moonstalker Fang Moonstalker Runt 20 % , Moonstalker Matriarch 20 % , Moonstalker Sire 20 % , Moonstalker 20 %","desc":"The Buzzbox gives a burst of static as you hear Wizbang begin to speak.\n\"The next Buzzbox is number 323. Ish north of Auberdine but... where's the ale? Wha? Oh, ish on the road sho ya shouldn't have trouble finding it near the bridge.\"\nWizbang mumbles something incoherent before you hear a loud gulping sound.\n\"Thish one needs Moonstalker Fangs... 6 of 'em.\"","rew":"Money: 6 0 gold, 6 silver, 0 copper Experience: 975\n+100 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Though you have yet to place the 6 Moonstalker Fangs inside, you believe you hear the sounds of static and incoherent gnome ramblings coming from within. Could someone else have fixed the machine already?","done":"The Buzzbox suddenly leaps into action, and you can hear the distinct sounds of teeth being ground to dust coming from within.\n\"Sho, ya made it! Thatsh exshellent newsh... Sho... Why doncha move along? Oh! Unless you want another job!\"","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":42,"y":28.6,"n":"Buzzbox 411","s":1},{"z":"Darkshore","x":51.3,"y":24.6,"n":"Buzzbox 323","e":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"4762":{"id":4762,"t":"The Cliffspring River","lv":15,"min":11,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel north of Auberdine to the first waterfall along the Cliffspring River and draw a sample from the pool there.\nReturn to Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine with the Cliffspring River Sample.\nCliffspring River Sample\nProvided: Empty Sampling Tube","desc":"The Cliffspring River has begun turning foul and corrupted. It empties into the Mist's Edge, and I fear the wash will affect Auberdine soon. I suspect the Blackwood furbolgs up-river are the cause of the taint, but I also suspect that they aren't the true root of it.\nTake this sampling tube and go to the mouth of the river to our north. Proceed inland to the first waterfall and draw a sample from the pool there. You'll see a bridge overhead. Once you have a sample, return to me in Auberdine.","rew":"Experience: 800\n+75 reputation with Darnassus","back":"The pollution of the Cliffspring River is but the start of an alarming trend here in Darkshore. The sample you provide will help us formalize a plan... a plan of attack, I am starting to suspect.","done":"It's no surprise how tainted this water is, but just look at how putrid it is becoming! It would seem that action is needed sooner than later, eh ‹name›?\nTo our east is Felwood; it is the real source of this corruption, one that I have seen in times past. I predict this sample will confirm this. We might be able to enact a cure for it here, but in order to even try we will need assistance. When that time comes ‹name›, I hope you will be able to give the aid we need.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":37.4,"y":40.1,"n":"Thundris Windweaver","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"98042":{"id":98042,"t":"Its all fun and games until","lv":17,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Obtain a Peerless Eye from a Twilight Disciple or Thug at the Master's Glaive in Darkshore and find someone in Auberdine who is willing to take it.\nPeerless Eye","desc":"<As you tear away the single page from the Twilight Tome, a foreboding voice floods your mind, uninvited.>\nThey have failed.\nYou will be forgotten.\nThey will lose the eye they gained.","rew":"Money: 9 0 gold, 9 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,250\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"You look troubled. I am listening.","done":"<Thundris does not speak for some time.>\nThis bears the mark of an ancient evil, ‹class›. I will see it brought to Darnassus at once for further study.\nAnde'thoras-ethil.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":38.6,"y":86.1,"n":"Twilight Tome","s":1},{"z":"Darkshore","x":37.4,"y":40.2,"n":"Thundris Windweaver","e":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"6762":{"id":6762,"t":"Rabine Saturna","lv":55,"min":54,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Rabine Saturna in the village of Nighthaven, Moonglade. Moonglade lies between Felwood and Winterspring, accessible through a path out of Timbermaw Hold.","desc":"For this task, Keeper Remulos' majordomo in Moonglade - Rabine Saturna - seeks aid in exploring the vast wastelands far to the west of Tanaris... and even further west of Un'Goro. You should find him in Nighthaven, the main village of Moonglade.\nWhile your work will no doubt be of tremendous benefit to us all, I advise you to tread gingerly. There are tensions between Darnassus and Moonglade... ones that may grow over the course of time.","rew":"Experience: 1,400\n+25 reputation with Cenarion Circle","done":"I am Rabine Saturna, and on behalf of Keeper Remulos and all of the denizens of this sacred glade I bid you welcome.\nI appreciate your interest and eagerness to assist the Cenarion Circle. I also know that Arch Druid of Darnassus expressed his displeasure to you in your lending us aid. Rest assured that it is for the greater good, and that you will be safe from any ill-conceived repercussions you may be the target of.\nYou are among friends here, ‹name›.\nDarnassus Moonglade","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":35.4,"y":8.4,"n":"Mathrengyl Bearwalker","s":1},{"z":"Moonglade","x":51.7,"y":45.1,"n":"Rabine Saturna","e":1}],"cats":["darnassus"]},"1482":{"id":1482,"t":"The Corrupter","lv":35,"min":25,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring an Oracle Crystal to Maurin Bonesplitter in Desolace.\nOracle Crystal Slitherblade Oracle","desc":"An oracle crystal would do nicely. They are crafted by the naga for their oracles to use.\nNorthwest of here, along the coast, is a vast coral reef that the naga have taken as their home when this close to the shore. You can find their oracles there. The Slitherblade are deadly and will not react kindly to your intrusions, so be careful and make haste.\nWhen you return, we shall see about finding this demon lord Azrethoc.","rew":"Experience: 2,750\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"I am ready for the oracle crystal, ‹class›. Finding and destroying this Lord Azrethoc would garner a great deal of favor with the Warchief for both of us. We would do well to work together and to do so swiftly so we may further our own ends and curry favor with the Warchief.","done":"A precious oracle crystal... flawless... beautiful. Indeed.\nWe shall begin immediately. Finding this demon lord should be our primary concern, and its slaying demands our utmost attention.\nTake a step back, ‹class›, and let us see what this demon is, and where he may be found.","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":52.2,"y":53.4,"n":"Maurin Bonesplitter","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"7482":{"id":7482,"t":"Elven Legends","lv":60,"min":54,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 8,300 experience instead of 8,550, 0.97 times as much.","obj":"Search Dire Maul for Kariel Winthalus. Report back to Scholar Runethorn at Feathermoon with whatever information that you may find.","desc":"Several years ago, a lone elven master named Kariel Winthalus fled the devastation of his homeland with several ancient elven artifacts in tow.\nOur search for this lost master lead us from the ruins of Quel'Thalas, through the Burning Steppes, across the great expanses of the sea, to Feralas.\nWe suspect that the elf sought sanctuary in the halls of Eldre'Thalas (what is now known as Dire Maul).\nYou must find him, adventurer. Whether alive or dead, the knowledge he carried must be recovered!","rew":"Money: 1 80 1 gold, 80 silver, 0 copper Experience: 8,300","back":"My associate, the tauren sage, Korolusk, is recruiting his allies for this task.","done":"A shame... a tragedy. The items are lost you say? No trace of him, eh?","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":31.2,"y":43.9,"n":"Scholar Runethorn","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dire-maul"]},"6122":{"id":6122,"t":"The Principal Source","lv":14,"min":14,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Empty Cliffspring Falls Sampler to draw a sample of water from the mouth of the cave by the falls.\nDeliver the Filled Cliffspring Falls Sampler to Alanndarian Nightsong in Auberdine, Darkshore.\nFilled Cliffspring Falls Sampler\nProvided: Empty Cliffspring Falls Sampler","desc":"The Cliffspring Falls in Darkshore serves as the principal source of drinking water for the region, and now I suspect it is the principal source of the poison that is harming the local fauna - deer specifically. Use this sampler to draw some water from the mouth of the cave; be careful, as dangerous naga now reside in a cave by the falls.\nOnce filled, deliver it to Alanndarian Nightsong in Auberdine. She is the one that requested our aid, and you will work with her to address this malady.","rew":"Experience: 750\n+75 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"You're the one that the Cenarion Circle in Moonglade sent? That's wonderful! We've quite the crisis our hands here regarding the poor deer, and we're happy for all the help we can get.\nDo you have the sample of water that Dendrite Starblaze said you'd have? He notified me that you'd draw one so we could work on a cure together...","done":"By Elune, this water is disgusting! No wonder the deer are sick.\nSomething is polluting the water, and in turn corrupting Darkshore's entire water table. Sick deer have been seen all over area, and not just by the river. While this water is most likely a primary source of the sickness spreading, there's something else at work here.\nThis water, believe it or not, will help us formulate a cure. While I research this water, I have need of some items to formulate a cure...\nMoonglade Darkshore","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":56.2,"y":30.6,"n":"Dendrite Starblaze","s":1},{"z":"Darkshore","x":37.7,"y":40.7,"n":"Alanndarian Nightsong","e":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"98362":{"id":98362,"t":"To thunder bluff","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Return to Thunder Bluff and speak with Turak Runetotem on the Elder Rise.","desc":"The time has come for us to part ways once again, young one, as the application of your lessons takes you back to whom that sent you to me. It would seem your instructor, Turak Runetotem, has found a worthy pupil in you. I believe I see one as well. Heed his lessons and you shall soon be able to draw upon the Great Cat Spirit to take its shape.\nGo back to whence you came. When the time is right, we will meet again.","done":"Welcome back, Cory. I can sense you have met with the Great Cat Spirit and have successfully completed the trial. All druids must pass a trial given by this spirit, though the trials vary by generation. I am proud you have passed and have heeded the wisdom of the Great Cat Spirit. It is an ancient spirit that is as deadly as it is playful, though I can sense you understand the spirit's nature already.\nI will now instruct you on how to take the shape of the cat.\nMoonglade Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":56.2,"y":30.4,"n":"Dendrite Starblaze","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":76.4,"y":27.6,"n":"Turak Runetotem","e":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"282":{"id":282,"t":"Senir's Observations","lv":5,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Mountaineer Thalos.\nGrelin's Report\nProvided: Grelin's Report","desc":"I was planning on sending my apprentice to my brother Senir with my report, but I would feel much better were it placed in more... reliable hands. That is, of course, if you wouldn't mind?\nHmm... you'll have to take the tunnel to get to Kharanos.\nSpeak with Mountaineer Thalos before going through the tunnel. It's completely infested with troggs now.\nFollow the road back to Anvilmar, then keep heading east to the tunnel, Thalos is stationed nearby.","rew":"Experience: 340\n+75 reputation with Ironforge\n+75 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Hail! Have a care, ‹name›, the tunnel to Dun Morogh is infested with troggs and is not safe for travel.\nIf you haven't any pressing business in Dun Morogh, I'll have to ask you to remain in Anvilmar until the tunnel is safer.","done":"Hm, well, if Whitebeard is sending you to Dun Morogh on important business, I can't very well stop you, can I?\nAt least let me provide you with some advice and directions.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":25.1,"y":75.7,"n":"Grelin Whitebeard","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":33.5,"y":71.8,"n":"Mountaineer Thalos","e":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"99162":{"id":99162,"t":"Treacherous cold","lv":8,"min":5,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect the rifles of fallen mountaineers.\nStoneanvil's Rifle\nSunhammer's Rifle\nCoalbeard's Rifle","desc":"Even mountaineers from Ironforge have to keep their wits about them when traversing through the peaks of Dun Morogh. Falling snow and ice often spells the end of some more novice members' lives.\nAfter a slide, I usually try to find any sign of survivors or victims--while praying to the Light that there's nothing to be found. But with the elements acting up, I've held off wandering too far. If you could look for some lost mountaineers and bring me their rifles, I will return them to Ironforge.","back":"What do you need?","done":"The mountaineers engrave their names on the stock of their rifles. It helps identify them should something happen. I'll send these back to Ironforge--there someone will pass them on to any family.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":57.6,"y":44.8,"n":"Father Gavin","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"842":{"id":842,"t":"Crossroads Conscription","lv":12,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Follow the western road from Kargal's Far Watch Outpost.\nAt the T intersection, turn left and follow the road south.\nFind Sergra Darkthorn at the crossing of roads within the Crossroads.\nSigned Recruitment Letter\nProvided: Signed Recruitment Letter","desc":"Take this signed recruitment letter to the Crossroads.\nSergra Darkthorn, curse her hide, is in charge there. She's a nasty shaman who will talk your head in circles before she lets you do anything useful. Thrall is convinced she's something special, but I'm not so sure.\nYou'll just have to decide for yourself, pup...","rew":"Experience: 900\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Well well well, what do we have here? Has Kargal deemed me worthy of another recruit?","done":"Alright, ‹name›. You want to earn your keep with the Horde? Well there's plenty to do here, so listen close and do what you're told.\nI see that look in your eyes, do not think I will tolerate any insolence. Thrall himself has declared the Hordes females to be on equal footing with you men. Disrespect me in the slightest, and you will know true pain./I'm happy to have met you. Thrall will be glad to know that more females like you and I are taking the initiative to push forward in the Barrens.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.3,"y":19.4,"n":"Kargal Battlescar","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":52.2,"y":31,"n":"Sergra Darkthorn","e":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"1322":{"id":1322,"t":"The Black Shield","lv":37,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Acquire 5 Acidic Venom Sacs for Do'gol in Brackenwall Village.\n5 Acidic Venom Sac Darkmist Recluse 25 % , Darkfang Lurker 25 % , Darkfang Spider 25 % , Darkfang Venomspitter 25 % and 4 more","desc":"Hmmm, there's writing right here on the rim of the shield, but it's hard to read from all the burned stuff.\nI need acid to make it clear. Venom from the darkmist spiders would do good. The spiders have taken over an old mine, the Darkmist Cavern, northwest of the village. Get me some of their sacs and I can clean this up.","rew":"Experience: 2,850","back":"Did you get them sacs from the spiders?","done":"I don't like spiders that are so big I can't sit on them and squish them.\nThanks for getting them, ‹name›. Now I rip them open and pour them onto the shield...","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":36.5,"y":30.8,"n":"Do'gol","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"6042":{"id":6042,"t":"Un-Life's Little Annoyances","lv":58,"min":54,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Slay 20 Noxious Plaguebats and 10 Monstrous Plaguebats. Return to Nathanos Blightcaller when you are finished.\nNoxious Plaguebat slain : 0/ 20\nMonstrous Plaguebat slain : 0/ 10","desc":"You cannot take two steps off of this farm without running into one of those obnoxious bats. I want to be able to take the hounds out and slaughter Scourge without being accosted by any damned, dirty bats. Obviously, I have better things to do with my time than mindlessly kill bats day in and day out. You, however, do not.\nWhat? Your training? This is your training! Now get out of my sight and don't come back until you've killed a fair number of those winged demons. Don't disappoint me.","rew":"Money: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,200\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"It could have been worse. I could have had you collecting bat guano.\n<Nathanos stares at you in contemplation.>\nHrm... Hey! Wait a minute. Where are you going?","done":"It's incredible what a little anger and rage can get accomplished.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":22.2,"y":63.5,"n":"Nathanos Blightcaller","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"7962":{"id":7962,"t":"Wabbit pelts","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring 3 LeCrafty Rabbit Pelts to Jon LeCraft.\n3 LeCraft Rabbit Pelt","desc":"I want LeCrafty rabbit pelts. Get me some from LeCrafty Rabbits.\nThis is important!","rew":"You will receive:\n22 Pound Lobster\nMoney: 30 0 gold, 0 silver, 30 copper Experience: 100\n+150 reputation with Stormwind\nLevel 1 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 4 6 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 7962","cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"3642":{"id":3642,"t":"The Pledge of Secrecy","lv":47,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"If you agree to become a Gnome Engineer, then right-click on the Pledge of Secrecy and speak once more with Oglethrope Obnoticus in Booty bay.\nOglethorpe's Signed Pledge\nProvided: Oglethorpe's Pledge of Secrecy","desc":"Gnome engineering is about engineering theory shaped to serve our needs! Our schemata allow us to make devices that control the world around us; the manual you read covered this.\nThe manual also covered our ages old oath of secrecy on our schemata. Once you become a gnome engineer, that's that. There is no access to goblin engineering at all.\nIf you still want to become a gnome engineer, sign this document pledging life-long secrecy and speak with me again. Think about it carefully, ‹name›.","rew":"Experience: 420","back":"If you've signed the document and are ready to hand it to me, then that is that.\nWhile I may vehemently disagree with Gnomeregan - especially that fool Tinkmaster Overspark - politically, the Pledge of Secrecy transcends everything else! You must agree to commit a single path and stay true to that path throughout your life.","done":"Welcome aboard, ‹name›! You soon will have access to the most advanced engineering schemata anywhere on Azeroth.\nNow that you have committed yourself to the pursuit of this knowledge, it is time to examine your gnome-oriented engineering work. From there, we'll help you build a plan to maximize your gnome engineering talents!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":28.4,"y":76.4,"n":"Oglethorpe Obnoticus","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["engineering"]},"4442":{"id":4442,"t":"Purified!","lv":54,"min":49,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Eridan again in a moment.","desc":"Using the water of Elune, I will attempt to purify the flute. We must end this suffering...\nMay Elune guide my hands and heart.\nSpeak with me again in a moment.","rew":"You will receive:\nFlute of the Ancients\nExperience: 5,450","done":"With the blessed water, I was able to break the link between the flute and the ancient spirit. I do believe though, that if you were to use this flute in a sacred spot, you may be able to summon the ancient spirits.\nPerhaps you might try the ruins in the southern part of Irontree Woods. Many corrupted treants inhabited this area at one time, and it is possible that they may still reside there, even in spirit form.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":51.3,"y":81.5,"n":"Eridan Bluewind","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"5882":{"id":5882,"t":"Salve via Hunting","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"6 Corrupted Soul Shard Ulathek 35 % , Xavaric 35 % , Prince Xavalis 35 % , Jaedenar Legionnaire 35 % and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\n2 Cenarion Plant Salve\nExperience: 4,200","back":"Possessing a Cenarion Beacon allows one to see a corrupted soul shard on those tainted beasts that are put down for the greater good. I grind shards into a usable reagent that goes into making Cenarion plant salve. We will use that salve to turn corrupted plants into healthy ones again.\nIn exchange for these shards, I will give you some Cenarion plant salves I have already prepared.","done":"Very well then, here are your Cenarion plant salves. Scour Felwood for corrupted plants, ‹name›! Wherever they are, use the salve I have given you to purify them.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":54.1,"y":86.8,"n":"Arathandris Silversky","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"5242":{"id":5242,"t":"A Final Blow","lv":58,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill Moora and Salia, and bring Shadow Lord Fel'dan's Head to Greta Mosshoof in Felwood.\nShadow Lord Fel'dan's Head Shadow Lord Fel'dan\nMoora slain\nSalia slain","desc":"Unfortunately, I see the only way to stop this threat to Felwood is a frontal attack. There are no other ways into Shadow Hold, and I have no means to teleport you inside. The straight path down to the bottom is the only way... and I also know who you should seek out. His name is Fel'dan... Shadow Lord Fel'dan. He is the mortal in power down below... he is the head of the serpent. Kill him and his two succubus servants and return to me. Fel'dan is the one making pacts with the Legion. He must be stopped.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBrantwood Sash Blight Leather Gloves Gearforge Girdle\nExperience: 9,300","back":"Without Fel'dan, the Shadow Council will hopefully lose focus and start infighting. They will struggle with one another for control and hoard assets for future plans. That will be an opportune time to devastate them and their demon slaves.","done":"Earthmother be praised, ‹name›! Thank you! This is a great day, indeed!\nThe Shadow Council will be hard pressed to scale to the same levels of power they once held with this blow to their hierarchy. You have done a great thing this day!","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":51.2,"y":82.1,"n":"Greta Mosshoof","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"3002":{"id":3002,"t":"The Gordunni Orb","lv":47,"min":38,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Gordunni Orb to Uthel'nay in the Darkbriar Lodge in Orgrimmar.\nGordunni Orb Gordunni Mage-Lord\nProvided: Gordunni Orb","desc":"Although I know my enemy well, I am a warrior, ‹name›. I cannot begin to tell you what this orb is capable of.\nI know of a mage in Orgrimmar that will be able to tell us more about the orb. Take it to him.","rew":"Experience: 2,100\n+50 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"What have you brought me, ‹race›?","done":"Fascinating, ‹name›...\nThis orb is very powerful, but also very dangerous.\nFeralas Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":75.8,"y":43.6,"n":"Rok Orhan","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":39.2,"y":86.3,"n":"Uthel'nay","e":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"2922":{"id":2922,"t":"Save Techbot's Brain!","lv":26,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 4,750 experience instead of 2,650, 1.79 times as much. Read from what the game server sent. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved what dungeon quests give beyond a normal quest.","obj":"Bring Techbot's Memory Core to Tinkmaster Overspark in Ironforge.\nTechbot's Memory Core Techbot","desc":"When our beloved city Gnomeregan fell, a rogue spark must have jolted my poor creation, Techbot. It once aided me and my associates with its countless gizmos and limitless store of information, but its positronic brain has polarized. Now it's negatronic... and Techbot's behaviors are reversed. It roams Gnomeregan in a frenzy!\nBut perhaps it can be salvaged. Perhaps, if you can retrieve Techbot's memory core and bring it to me, I can discover the cause of the polarization and fix my poor Techbot.","rew":"Money: 20 0 gold, 20 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,750\n+150 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Did you find Techbot? Did you retrieve its memory core??","done":"Oh, this is wonderful! Thank you, ‹name›! I'll get to work immediately!!\nPoor, poor Techbot... Don't feel bad. We'll get you fixed.\nNow, where did I put that plug for my hydro-jack swivel spanner...","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.2,"y":29.2,"n":"Tinkmaster Overspark","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["gnomeregan"]},"4602":{"id":4602,"t":"The Sparklematic 5200!","lv":30,"min":25,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -1g -3s instead of 0.","obj":"Insert a Grime-Encrusted Item into the Sparklematic 5200, and be sure to have three silver coins to start the machine.\nGrime-Encrusted Object Holdout Technician 25 % , Holdout Medic 25 % , Holdout Warrior 25 % , Irradiated Pillager 25 % and 4 more","desc":"This contraption stands out amongst the gnomes holding out against the madness outside the room. A small plaque on the device reads \"The Sparklematic 5200\", followed by some text:\n\"Grime and residue ruining your sparklies? The Sparklematic 5200 puts the shine back in shine-tastic! Insert the item you wish to clean and deposit three silver coins in the coin slot. Give the Sparklematic 5200 a moment for operation, and voila! Your valuables will emerge clean and shiny!\"","back":"It would seem that the device needs some sort of grime-encrusted object to clean and three silver coins to get the contraption working. So long as both are present, the Sparklematic 5200 should work...","done":"You insert the grime-encrusted item and three silver coins into the Sparklematic 5200. The machine surges to life in an almost frenzied attempt to purge the grime from the unknown item. Loud, violent churning sounds beat from the heart of the machine. The metal frame of the beast creaks and groans as it lurches from side to side...\nStart The Sparklematic 5200 End The Sparklematic 5200 Level 30 , requires level 25 Difficulty 25 26 28 33 38 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable Yes Quest ID 4602\nThe chain\n3 quests at level 30, 2,450 XP in all.\n1 [ 30 ] The Sparklematic 5200! this quest\nInsert a Grime-Encrusted Item into the Sparklematic 5200, and be sure to have three silver coins to start the machine.\nThe Sparklematic 5200\n2 [ 30 ] The Sparklematic 5200!\nThe Sparklematic 5200\n2,450 XP\n3 [ 30 ] More Sparklematic Action\nThe Sparklematic 5200","cats":["gnomeregan"]},"2842":{"id":2842,"t":"Chief Engineer Scooty","lv":35,"min":25,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 20 instead of 25. Partly read from what the game server sent.","obj":"Speak with Scooty in Booty Bay.","desc":"As soon as we got word from Kernobee about the new gnomish rig, Scooty and I began work on the Transpolyporter 6000: The fastest and most reliable way to Gnomeregan.\nIt's finally ready for passengers to board, ‹name›. If you want to give it a try, go to Booty Bay and talk with Scooty at the wind rider roost. To get to Booty Bay, take the boat from Ratchet.\nOf course, you could always try and make the run to Gnomeregan through the dwarf infested mountains of Dun Morogh!","rew":"Experience: 280","done":"She's a beauty, isn't she? Pinnacle of goblin transport technology -- only exploded a dozen or so times.\nDon't worry, ‹name›, I've got her all fixed up. She won't blow up on you - and if she does, it'll be quick and painless.\nOrgrimmar Stranglethorn Vale","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":75.5,"y":25.4,"n":"Sovik","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27.6,"y":77.5,"n":"Scooty","e":1}],"cats":["gnomeregan"]},"3082":{"id":3082,"t":"Etched Tablet","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Jen'shan in the Valley of Trials.\nEtched Tablet\nProvided: Etched Tablet","desc":"Ah, while you were gone a tablet came for you, ‹name›.\nRead it when you have time. If I'm not mistaken, it came from the hunter trainer Jen'shan. She would have words with you when you're ready.","rew":"Experience: 40\n+50 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Jen'shan see a mighty ‹class› before her and da spirits approve.\nDa path of da ‹class› is one of our oldest walks of life. Da Horde turned to us when they be just strugglin' to survive on Azeroth, and they ask us to teach them, to show them the secrets of many tings. They were strong already: strong in shaman ways; strong in warrior ways. But the hunter path not be their path... then.","done":"Now we teach them those things, and they teach us others. We become one race... almost. We be allies for long time now. So you remember to help them. And Jen'shan remember to help you.\nJen'shan teach you da ways of the hunter--teach you good. You never forget, ‹class›'s be respected greatly by da tribe. You be havin' a large role to play in da future... you never forget that.\nWhen you feel da need, come to Jen'shan. She teach you as much as she can when she feel you ready.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":42.1,"y":68.3,"n":"Gornek","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":42.8,"y":69.3,"n":"Jen'shan","e":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"7802":{"id":7802,"t":"A Donation of Wool","lv":60,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"60 Wool Cloth Farrin Daris 66.7 % , Adam Lind 62.1 % , Mountaineer Langarr 57.1 % , Protector Leick 47.6 % and 4 more","rew":"Experience: 650\n+150 reputation with Ironforge","back":"We are currently accepting donations for wool cloth. A donation of sixty pieces of wool cloth will net you full recognition by Ironforge for your generous actions. Our stores are such on wool that we would only need sixty pieces from you total; we should be able to acquire enough from others in the realm to support our drive.\nIf you have the sixty pieces of wool cloth on you and are ready to donate them, I'm able to take them from you now.","done":"Wonderful! We thank you for your generous donation, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58,"y":26.2,"n":"Mistina Steelshield","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"9002":{"id":9002,"t":"Saving the Best for Last","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Give Deliana your Lightforge Helm and Lightforge Breastplate.\nLightforge Helm Darkmaster Gandling 0 %\nLightforge Breastplate General Drakkisath 0 %","desc":"That's an amazing story, ‹name›! You have my thanks, and the heartfelt gratitude of all who were involved. Now maybe I'll be able to sleep at night with both eyes shut.\nAs to your reward, I believe I have a few things that you'll really enjoy.","rew":"You will receive:\nSoulforge Helm Soulforge Breastplate\nExperience: 1,650","back":"As per our deal, are you ready to hand over your Lightforge pieces in exchange for your new Soulforge Helmet and Breastplate?","done":"I'm going to miss you, ‹name›. I owe you such a debt of gratitude; I think I'll never be able to repay it.\nI hope that you enjoy your new head and chest armor, and that it protects you for a long time to come.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58.1,"y":29.5,"n":"Deliana","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"8682":{"id":8682,"t":"Skyseer the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"Your spirit burns with life, young ‹class›. I accept the homage you pay, and offer in return this token...","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":45.3,"y":50,"n":"Elder Skyseer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"1882":{"id":1882,"t":"The Balnir Farmstead","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Balnir Snapdragons to Anastasia Hartwell in the Mage Quarter of the Undercity.\nBalnir Snapdragons Balnir Snapdragons","desc":"The Plaguelands to the east are an aberration. Devised by the Lich King, they spread their magic into the soil, corrupting and killing all that live. Although there is a certain charm to the destructive forces of the plague, we, the mages of the Forsaken, believe it is unruly and must be curtailed.\nBut first, we must measure how far it has spread into Tirisfal. Go to the Balnir Farmstead in eastern Tirisfal. In the garden are flowers--snapdragons. Gather these and return.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nArcane Orb Arcane Staff\nExperience: 850","back":"Do you have the snapdragons? That breed of flower is highly receptive to magic energies, and studying the snapdragons so close to the Plaguelands can tell us if the plague has entered Tirisfal Glades.","done":"Ah, a fine specimen this is. I will send it to be studied by our apothecaries to determine the extent of the Plagueland's taint.\nWell done, ‹name›. For your services, I present to you this choice: an orb or staff. Whichever you choose, you will find it quite useful.\nUndercity Tirisfal Glades","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":85.1,"y":10,"n":"Anastasia Hartwell","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"1962":{"id":1962,"t":"Spellfire Robes","lv":15,"min":15,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nLesser Spellfire Robes\nExperience: 1,050","done":"Here are your robes, ‹name›. Wear them well.","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":70.8,"y":30.7,"n":"Josef Gregorian","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"9322":{"id":9322,"t":"Wild Fires in Kalimdor","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 1 instead of 50.","obj":"Visit the Midsummer camps located in Azshara, Silithus, Un'Goro Crater, and Winterspring, then return to the Festival Flamekeeper.\nFlame of Azshara used\nFlame of Silithus used\nFlame of Un'Goro used\nFlame of Winterspring used","desc":"The Midsummer Fire Festival is celebrated everywhere in Azeroth, and the diverse land of Kalimdor is no exception. You look fit to travel -- perhaps a journey is in order.\nMidsummer cannot be truly appreciated unless you've seen the blistering blue fires abroad. The celebrants have lit fires in chilly western Winterspring, northeastern Azshara, near Valor's Rest in the wastes of Silithus, and by the entrance to lush Un'Goro. Return once your journey is complete.","rew":"You will receive:\nCinder Bracers 10 Burning Blossom\nExperience: 3,300","back":"Are the flames of Kalimdor burning brightly?","done":"Your spirit glows with the warmth of the Kalimdor fires, friend. Is the heat not invigorating? Once the power fades from you, perhaps these will help rekindle the feeling.\nOrgrimmar Tirisfal Glades Teldrassil Azshara Silithus Un'Goro Crater Winterspring","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":42.6,"y":34.2,"n":"Festival Flamekeeper","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.7,"y":72.7,"n":"Festival Flamekeeper","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":56.6,"y":91.9,"n":"Festival Flamekeeper","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["midsummer"]},"99082":{"id":99082,"t":"The high chieftain","lv":9,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Seek audience with High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof in Thunder Bluff.","desc":"Your bravery defending your people demands recognition. Journey to Thunder Bluff to the northwest, our mighty city whose shadow grants us shade in the warmer months, and seek audience with my father.\nIt was he who led the charge with the young Warchief Thrall to reclaim these plains and drive the centaur away for good. As High Chieftain, he will reward you generously for your part in ensuring his own bravery is honored.\nYou must take a lift to reach the High Chieftain, who sits on the central rise.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nProud Brave's Guard Centaur Skull Basher\nExperience: 80\n+10 reputation with Thunder Bluff","done":"The Galak centaur dare show themselves in Mulgore?!\nYou have brought pride to your ancestors by driving them out. Perhaps that will remind them of the pain that awaits them should they do so again!\nPlease accept this gift in honor of this. May it serve you well as you venture out into the Earth Mother's kingdom, to the far reaches of this world.\nMulgore Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":47.4,"y":60.2,"n":"Baine Bloodhoof","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":59.8,"y":51.6,"n":"Cairne Bloodhoof","e":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"9082":{"id":9082,"t":"Bonescythe Gauntlets","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Rohan the Assassin at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Bonescythe Gauntlets if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Gauntlets, 8 Wartorn Leather Scraps, 1 Arcanite Bar and 5 Cured Rugged Hides.\nDesecrated Gauntlets\n8 Wartorn Leather Scrap Skeletal Steed 26.1 % in Naxxramas , Necro Knight Guardian 26.1 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 24.5 % in Naxxramas , Stoneskin Gargoyle 24.1 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\nArcanite Bar\n5 Cured Rugged Hide","desc":"If you want Bonescythe made, you're going to have to supply the materials.\nEnter Naxxramas, the big floating city of death in the sky up there, and find desecrated armor and wartorn armor scraps. Bring those back along with the materials to put everything together and you'll have your Bonescythe. Oh, and you'll need to pay me for my troubles... I'll supply the bones.","rew":"You will receive:\nBonescythe Gauntlets\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"How do you expect me to get anything done without the items I requested?","done":"These gauntlets could probably substitute as weapons if absolutely necessary. Wear them with pride!","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.6,"y":48.9,"n":"Rohan the Assassin","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"9242":{"id":9242,"t":"Polar Gloves","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -200g instead of 0.","obj":"Craftsman Wilhelm at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 5 Frozen Runes, 12 Enchanted Leather, 3 Essence of Water, 3 Cured Rugged Hides and 200 gold.\n5 Frozen Rune Frozen Rune in Naxxramas\n12 Enchanted Leather sold by Lhara\n3 Essence of Water Princess Tempestria 70.6 % , Lord Skwol 53.3 % , Hydrospawn 11 % , Toxic Horror 7.2 % and 4 more\n3 Cured Rugged Hide","desc":"Thanks to you and Omarion (May he rest in peace), I am now able to create Polar gloves. All you need to do is bring me the materials and pay a small crafting fee.","rew":"You will receive:\nPolar Gloves","back":"Have you brought the materials?","done":"Here is your order, ‹name›. Delivered as promised!","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.2,"y":49.9,"n":"Craftsman Wilhelm","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"97242":{"id":97242,"t":"Yelmaks medley","lv":15,"min":9,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Take some cuttings from the Cattails and Speargrass growing around the water flows in the Valley of Honor and return to Kor'geld in Yelmak's Alchemy and Potions\n2 Handful of Cattails\n4 Speargrass Cuttings","desc":"Yelmak doesn't want his apprentice breaking anything. Well, anything more than he already has.\nHe told me the young mixer in training has too much pride to ask for help when he really needs it. Yelmak wants to give him a taste of a particular home-brewed recipe.\nGather a mix of cattail and speargrass cuttings taken from the plants growing around the water in the Valley of Honor. I'd get them myself, but if I left the shop, Whuut would surely know we're catering to his mood.","back":"We discover formulations and recipes by showing old ingredients to new generations, who experiment with it in their own way.","done":"This type of cattail and speargrass is unique to Orgrimmar. Drinking from Azshara mountain spring water, and nourished by the sweat and blood soaked mineral dust of our rocky land, these herbs contain potent powers locked within.\nI'll give these to Yelmak, who may be able to win back Whuut's ear with a hands-on lesson.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":56.2,"y":34.2,"n":"Kor'geld","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"1642":{"id":1642,"t":"The Tome of Divinity","lv":12,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Duthorian Rall in Stormwind.","desc":"In all things, a paladin must reflect the Light which supplements our strength. To strive to be divine for one of our kind does not mean we strive for godhood--we strive to be good in all actions.\nAlthough called upon to smite evil in these harsh times, you must always remember that it's aiding others that will truly set you apart from the citizens of Azeroth. Compassion, patience, bravery--these things mean as much to a paladin as strength in battle.\nKnow this well, and never forget it.","rew":"Experience: 90","done":"Hello again, ‹name›. How goes your studies of the Tome of Divinity?\nThen you should be prepared to have yourself tested. There are always tasks to be done throughout the city and our lands; acts of compassion and understanding; people who need help; creatures to slay.\nBy proving you have the patience to help others, especially those who are less fortunate, you prove that you are a servant of the Light and of sound mind.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":50.5,"y":47.5,"n":"Duthorian Rall","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"7642":{"id":7642,"t":"Collection of Goods","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -150g instead of 0.","obj":"Bring 40 Runecloth, 6 Arcanite Bars, 10 Arthas' Tears, 5 Stratholme Holy Water vials, and 150 gold to Grimand Elmore in the Dwarven District of Stormwind.\n5 Stratholme Holy Water Supply Crate in Stratholme , Stratholme Supply Crate in Stratholme\n10 Arthas' Tears Arthas' Tears in Razorfen Downs , Arthas' Tears , Spirit of Trey Lightforge 33.3 % , Treant Spirit 3.9 % and 4 more\n40 Runecloth Stormwind Royal Guard , Honor Guard , Skullsplitter Speaker in Zul'Gurub , General Marcus Jonathan 85.7 % and 4 more\n6 Arcanite Bar","desc":"You'll need four things for the barding - runecloth for the lining, arcanite bars for the plating, Arthas' Tears for the spiritual attunement, and Stratholme holy water for the spiritual imbuement. Actually, you need five things... gold for my fee. That fee includes all labor as well as a handcrafted saddle and stirrups.\nOnce you've got all that, I'll be able to finish your barding. Until then, there are some things I can get started on for you while you assemble your collection of goods.","rew":"Experience: 1,650\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Ah, ‹class›. I won't be able to finish your barding without the things I mentioned. Have you gotten everything together?","done":"This... well, this is exactly what I needed. You're quite the resourceful ‹class›, aren't you?\nAll right then, let's get this barding finished up for you!","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":59.7,"y":33.8,"n":"Grimand Elmore","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"5642":{"id":5642,"t":"Shadowguard","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Ur'kyo in Orgrimmar.","desc":"Something important is up in Orgrimmar, ‹name›.\nThe normal messengers that come through here looking for troll priests usually are very casual. This time, they seemed to be in much more a hurry. Don't dally too long in Thunder Bluff. I'd return to the Valley of Spirits as soon as possible.","rew":"You will learn: Shadowguard\nExperience: 390","done":"Your rites will come soon enough. For now, I teach you a spell that will be of great use to you when you do battle with your enemies.\nThunder Bluff Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":25.3,"y":15.3,"n":"Miles Welsh","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":35.6,"y":87.8,"n":"Ur'kyo","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"5722":{"id":5722,"t":"Searching for the Lost Satchel","lv":16,"min":9,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 1,800 experience instead of 875, 2.06 times as much. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved what dungeon quests give beyond a normal quest.","obj":"Search Ragefire Chasm for Maur Grimtotem's corpse and search it for any items of interest.","desc":"The troggs are not the only thing that interested Magatha in Ragefire Chasm. She has heard word that one of her servants, a Maur Grimtotem, found something peculiar while in the Chasm, but he never made it out to show her what. She'd like Maur's body found--if it still exists--and any signs of what he found while attempting to speak to the troggs.\nReturn to Magatha any items of interest, and I'm sure she would be very generous in her reward.\nAgain, seek the Chasm in the darkest areas of Orgrimmar.","rew":"Experience: 1,800","done":"The body looks seriously beaten by clubs or fists, but most of the corpse's clothing and equipment still looks present. It seems the troggs do not overly care much for material wealth.\nYou begin to search the body for anything of interest that might help Magatha.","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":70.1,"y":29.5,"n":"Rahauro","s":1}],"cats":["ragefire-chasm"]},"6522":{"id":6522,"t":"An Unholy Alliance","lv":36,"min":28,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 2,800 experience instead of 3,500, 0.8 times as much.","obj":"Take the Small Scroll to Varimathras in the Undercity.\nSmall Scroll Charlga Razorflank in Razorfen Kraul\nProvided: Small Scroll","desc":"My Lady,\nYou know very well what it is we are offering. The opportunity for you to take the Barrens and the lands beyond is a great one. We simply want your aid in return. By aid we mean nothing more than your giving us the freedom to take action in the area.\nPlease, allow us to discuss this further. We have great power and are willing to share with those wise enough to join us. I will remain outside Razorfen Downs for the time being.\nBest Regards,\nAmbassador Malcin","rew":"Money: 40 0 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,800","back":"What business is it you wish to speak of, ‹name›? You must feel it is important if you continue to pester me.","done":"I recognize the insignia on this scroll, ‹name›. You found this on that crone who reigns over Razorfen Kraul? Interesting.\nThe Scourge aren't content with one continent it seems. This Ambassador Malcin--the one who wrote the note--is one of the Scourge's plagued servants, a human diplomat to the kingdom of Lordaeron before things... changed.\nIf the Scourge are trying to gain a foothold in Kalimdor, then it is up to us to act.","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":56.3,"y":92.2,"n":"Varimathras","e":1}],"cats":["razorfen-downs"]},"122":{"id":122,"t":"Underbelly Scales","lv":18,"min":14,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Gather 6 Underbelly Whelp Scales from Black Dragon Whelps, and bring them to Verner Osgood in Redridge.\n6 Underbelly Whelp Scale Black Dragon Whelp 80 % , Snarlflare 80 %","desc":"I need some underbelly scales from black dragon whelps to pay for the shoes Argus sent me from Goldshire. If you can get 6 of them for me, then I can pay Argus with some... and have enough left to fashion something for you.\nBlack dragon whelps are often flying around south of Lakeshire, but they like to wander. You might have to just keep an eye out and hunt them when you see them.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBlack Whelp Boots Black Whelp Gloves\nExperience: 1,700\n+150 reputation with Stormwind","back":"I know that greedy Argus will send someone to collect his scales if I don't give them to him soon. Have you found those scales yet?","done":"Thanks! These will get me out of debt to Argus...","pins":[{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":25.9,"y":47.3,"n":"Verner Osgood","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["redridge-mountains"]},"8842":{"id":8842,"t":"One Commendation Signet","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Horde Commendation Signet","back":"For those adventurers who have but a single commendation signet, I'll exchange it for a small amount of recognition with Thunder Bluff.\nPlease bear in mind that it is better to hand over a stack of ten signets at once; your efforts will receive greater recognition in doing so. We offer a single signet exchange as a service for those who don't have enough for a full stack of ten.\nWith that being said, I stand ready to assist you if you still wish to hand in a single signet.","done":"Very well - your deeds have been entered into the records, and you are duly recognized for your efforts. Keep up the good work, ‹class›.\nIf you have any more signets to hand in, then I am able to assist you further in that regard.","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":42.4,"y":57,"n":"Officer Thunderstrider","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["reputation"]},"2282":{"id":2282,"t":"Alther's Mill","lv":20,"min":16,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 1,550 experience instead of 1,600, 0.97 times as much.","obj":"Open Lucius's Lockbox, recover the Token of Thievery and return it to Lucius in Lakeshire.\nToken of Thievery Lucius's Lockbox\nProvided: Thieves' Tools","desc":"We've been training thieves here for years! After all, not every rapscallion is born with the grace and finesse of old Lucius.\nUp off the road here you'll find Alther's Mill. I got a chest up there with something important inside. Go get it for me! Bring back that token and you'll receive your Certificate of Thievery!","rew":"You will receive:\nCertificate of Thievery\nExperience: 1,550","back":"Did I forget to mention the orcs?\nI hear they have been nosing around up by the mill.","done":"Cracked it open, did you? Nice work, ‹name›.\nIf you die now, we can rest easy knowing it was due to your own stupidity and not inexperience.","pins":[{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":23,"y":52,"n":"Lucius","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"7722":{"id":7722,"t":"What the Flux?","lv":50,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Somewhere in the Slag Pit of the Cauldron you will find the Secret Plans: Fiery Flux that Overseer Maltorius stole. Find those plans and return them to Master Smith Burninate in the Searing Gorge.\nSecret Plans: Fiery Flux Secret Plans: Fiery Flux","desc":"When that bastard, Maltorius, left our clan, he left with something more valuable than a pristine arcane crystal: Our recipe for fiery flux! I'd bet anything that the recipe was part of the deal in his new promotion amongst the Dark Irons.\nI want you to get our secret plans back, ‹name›. I'm sure they're somewhere near Maltorius, deep inside the Slag Pit.","rew":"Money: 75 0 gold, 75 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,700\n+100 reputation with Thorium Brotherhood","back":"Did you find the plans?","done":"I hope you kicked his teeth in too, ‹name›. Ragnaros knows, he deserved it.\nNow we can get down to business.","pins":[{"z":"Searing Gorge","x":38.8,"y":28.5,"n":"Master Smith Burninate","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["searing-gorge"]},"8762":{"id":8762,"t":"Metzen the Reindeer","lv":60,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Metzen the Reindeer. Use the notes provided to you for clues as to where he is being held.\nWhen you find Metzen, have the Pouch of Reindeer Dust in your possession so you can sprinkle some of the dust on him; this should free Metzen from his bonds of captivity.\nReturn the Pouch of Reindeer Dust to Wulmort Jinglepocket in Ironforge once Metzen is freed.\nPouch of Reindeer Dust Eldreth Spirit , Southsea Pirate , Shadowforge Digger , Glassweb Spider and 1 more\nFind Metzen the Reindeer and rescue him\nProvided: Smokywood Satchel","desc":"DISASTER has struck! Metzen the Reindeer has been kidnapped!\nMetzen is one of Greatfather Winter's eight reindeer - and property of Smokywood Pastures. We've received not one but TWO ransom letters from groups claiming to have Metzen. With the holiday season well under way, we're strapped to the coin box here! Please - find Metzen and return him to us!\nCheck out the ransom letters for clues, and sprinkle this reindeer dust on him - it will free him from any of his bonds!\nPlease, hurry!","rew":"You will receive:\n5 Preserved Holly\nExperience: 4,950\n+200 reputation with Steamwheedle Cartel","back":"‹name›! Were the notes in the satchel I gave you enough information to locate Metzen? I hate to think of what those cruel thugs might do to him... but there's no way we can afford to pay such an exorbitant ransom!","done":"You did it! Huzzah!\nMetzen flew back into Greatfather Winter's stables - yes Metzen can really fly - just a little while ago! The dust worked like a charm; I knew it would. You've saved the Feast of Winter Veil as well as Smokywood Pastures from disaster. Thank you, ‹name›.\nListen... because of what you've done here, I want you to have this. It's something VERY special; if you have a mount, I think you'll get a kick out of it. Happy Winter Veil!\nDun Morogh Searing Gorge Tanaris","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":56.5,"y":31.9,"n":"Wulmort Jinglepocket","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"8282":{"id":8282,"t":"Noggle's Lost Satchel","lv":58,"min":54,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Retrieve Noggle's Satchel from the mountains in the south of Silithus and return it to him at Cenarion Hold.\nNoggle's Satchel Noggle's Satchel","desc":"Where am I? Where's my bag? *gasp* I must've lost it while fleeing from Deathclasp, the giant scorpid. In my rush to escape I walked right into a nest of stonelash flayers.\nThe satchel I was carrying had all sorts of rare reagents in it. Without them, me and Beetix won't be able to make the potions that Cenarion Hold needs. I'm too weak to get up yet, but I can make it worth your while if you bring back my reagents.\nI ran into Deathclasp in the southern mountain range, behind Bronzebeard's camp.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\n2 Elixir of the Mongoose 2 Elixir of the Sages\nExperience: 6,200\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Still haven't found my bag? Well I should count my lucky stars, at least the poison's been cleansed.","done":"Yes! You brought my satchel back. And my rare reagents are all here! I'll be in your debt for a long time.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":51.6,"y":38.5,"n":"Noggle Ficklespragg","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8362":{"id":8362,"t":"Abyssal Crests","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"3 Abyssal Crest Crimson Templar , Azure Templar , Hoary Templar , Earthen Templar","rew":"You will receive:\nBag of Spoils\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"You've proved you can handle yourself in a fight, ‹name›. Let's keep the pressure up on the Twilight's Hammer. Go fight some more Abyssal Templars, I'll reward you with some of the stuff Huum and I have found in battle.","done":"You've done well! That's less Templars for me to worry about.\nHere you go, ‹name›. Hope there's something useful in there for you.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":48.6,"y":37.8,"n":"Bor Wildmane","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"442":{"id":442,"t":"Assault on Fenris Isle","lv":24,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Gnollhide Pants, Gnoll Shackles. Read from what the game server sent.","obj":"Bring Thule's Head to High Executor Hadrec at the Sepulcher.\nThule's Head Thule Ravenclaw","desc":"Now is the time to assault the Scourge's place of strength in Silverpine: Fenris Isle.\nYou must again go to the Isle and destroy Thule Ravenclaw. I want his head!\nThis mission is as dangerous as it is vital, ‹name›. You must not fail.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nHigh Robe of the Adjudicator Talonstrike Gnollhide Pants Gnoll Shackles\nNew in Forever: Gnollhide Pants, Gnoll Shackles.\nExperience: 1,950\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"The Scourge cannot be allowed to remain in Silverpine, ‹name›. Come back to me when you have proof of Thule's death.","done":"The death of Thule Ravenclaw was no small event, ‹name›. Renferrel tells me that the energies released when you destroyed Thule were felt even as far as the Sepulcher.\nYour actions ring through the ranks of the Forsaken. Your value to us grows.","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":43.4,"y":40.9,"n":"High Executor Hadrec","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"1082":{"id":1082,"t":"Update for Sentinel Thenysil","lv":22,"min":17,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Sentinel Thenysil in Ashenvale.","desc":"‹name›, you have done a great deed by lending a hand here.\nThe Sentinels of Ashenvale will reward you well if you informed them that Gaxim and I are alive. Tell them we are well on our way to stopping the Venture Co. and healing the lands.\nFind Tara Thenysil in Astranaar; she will be pleased to see you've returned with good news.","rew":"Experience: 875\n+50 reputation with Darnassus","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. You have done a service to the Sentinels.\nI'm glad to see Kaela... and even Gaxim, are doing well.\nYou've earned our appreciation.\nStonetalon Mountains Ashenvale","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":59.9,"y":66.8,"n":"Kaela Shadowspear","s":1},{"z":"Ashenvale","x":34.9,"y":49.8,"n":"Sentinel Thenysil","e":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"6282":{"id":6282,"t":"Harpies Threaten","lv":26,"min":18,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Maggran Earthbinder in Sun Rock Retreat wants you to slay 7 Bloodfury Harpies, 7 Bloodfury Ambushers, 7 Bloodfury Slayers and 7 Bloodfury Roguefeathers.\nBloodfury Harpy slain : 0/ 7\nBloodfury Ambusher slain : 0/ 7\nBloodfury Slayer slain : 0/ 7\nBloodfury Roguefeather slain : 0/ 7","desc":"Tauren take pride as the protector of these lands. Undoubtedly you can guess why I am alarmed with the number of harpies that dwell here in Stonetalon.\nThe Bloodfuries are the source of the increasing number of harpies in Kalimdor; they encroach upon all likes of life preventing the innocent from leaving their boundaries.\nI need you to cull the harpies, ‹name›!","rew":"Money: 20 0 gold, 20 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,100\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Do not be weary of Charred Vale; many evil creatures reside in those hills. Stay strong ‹name›, and you shall prevail over this threat to our people. Go now and strike hard - our children shall never know of the evil of what was.","done":"This is most excellent news! Tell me again how you cast fear into the cold hearts of those vile harpies. The Bloodfuries have been dealt a serious blow!","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":47.2,"y":61.2,"n":"Maggran Earthbinder","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"1242":{"id":1242,"t":"The Missing Diplomat","lv":28,"min":28,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Delivery Jorgen's Sealed Note to Elling Trias in Stormwind City.\nSealed Note to Elling\nProvided: Sealed Note to Elling","desc":"Take this here note to Elling Trias. Don't say nothin' else to him. Just be polite and wait for him to respond. And don't worry, he will.\nI'm gonna only impress this on ya once more, ‹name›: treat this matter seriously, and keep your yapper shut.\nYa can find Trias at his cheese shop, Trias' Cheese, in the Trade District. Good luck.","rew":"Experience: 230","back":"Hello, ‹name›. Is there something I can do for you? Perhaps you'd like to try some of our special Trias cheddar? Or a block of Darnassian bleu?","done":"I'm sorry, a letter for me? Well, I'll be... not often you get a delivery that's not a crate or barrel when all you do is work. Let's see what this is about.\n<Elling looks up at you while he opens the letter.>\nYou look a little tense, you okay, ‹name›?","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":76.3,"y":85.1,"n":"Jorgen","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":66,"y":74.1,"n":"Elling Trias","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"602":{"id":602,"t":"Magical Analysis","lv":37,"min":32,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the water elemental bracers to Archmage Ansirem Runeweaver in Dalaran.\nBag of Water Elemental Bracers\nProvided: Bag of Water Elemental Bracers","desc":"From what I've heard, the mages of Dalaran are busy with the reconstruction of their destroyed city, I'm sure you can find one of them who will spare some time to look at the bracers. If there's anything I know about mages, they can't resist a magical puzzle.\nTake the bag of water elemental bracers and see if they can shed any light on the Stone's curse. Look for the Archmage Ansirem Runeweaver in particular. I've dealt with him before, and his knowledge is vast.","rew":"Experience: 1,400\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","back":"If you wouldn't mind, I am rather busy right now.","done":"The Stone of the Tides? Most interesting. It might surprise you to know that I wrote a tome - several years ago - pertaining to the legends of the Gurubashi Empire. I do know quite a bit about the Stone.\nAt least one of these bracers appears to have some magical residue I can analyze.\nLet's see what I can see...\nStranglethorn Vale Alterac Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27.2,"y":76.9,"n":"Baron Revilgaz","s":1},{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":18.8,"y":78.5,"n":"Archmage Ansirem Runeweaver","e":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"202":{"id":202,"t":"Colonel Kurzen","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Madman's Blade, Dark Hearted Hammer.","obj":"Kill 6 Kurzen Elite, 4 Kurzen Subchiefs, and bring Kurzen's Head to Lieutenant Doren at the Rebel Camp.\nKurzen's Head Colonel Kurzen\nKurzen Elite slain : 0/ 6\nKurzen Subchief slain : 0/ 4","desc":"You have proven yourself time and again, and your resourcefulness seems to rival even that of Kurzen himself. You may be the salvation of our band of rebels...if you can pit yourself against Kurzen and prevail!\nHe commands his men from deep within the Stockpile. You must enter that cave, brave through his defenders, and face Kurzen and his leaders.\nFarewell, ‹name›. My hope, and the fate of my men, go with you.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nShrapnel Blaster Madman's Blade Dark Hearted Hammer\nNew in Forever: Madman's Blade, Dark Hearted Hammer.\nExperience: 3,150\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Dare I hope that Kurzen and his defenders are dead, ‹name›?","done":"I dared not believe the reports, but you bring us proof that... Kurzen and his leaders are defeated. You have saved us!\nThese jungles are filled with menaces of all types, but none had the cruel intellect of Kurzen. We may all breathe easier now that he is gone.\nStranglethorn Vale Duskwood","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":38,"y":3,"n":"Lieutenant Doren","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"3402":{"id":3402,"t":"The Undermarket","lv":50,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 40 instead of 43. Gives 4,700 experience instead of 6,750, 0.7 times as much.","obj":"Speak with Vizzklick in Gadgetzan.","desc":"I want you to personally deliver the news of Kovic's defeat to Vizzklick in Gadgetzan. He will be so happy to hear that Kovic is dead that I'm certain he'll give you some grand reward.","rew":"You will receive:\nPattern: Shadoweave Mask\nMoney: 75 0 gold, 75 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,700","done":"Kovic slain??! This is a glorious day, ‹name›! For years that scoundrel has been running shady undermarket trades, undercutting honest, hard working traders all over the world.\nYou deserve a fine reward for this accomplishment! And a fine reward you shall have!\nSearing Gorge Tanaris","pins":[{"z":"Searing Gorge","x":41,"y":74.9,"n":"Nilith Lokrav","s":1},{"z":"Tanaris","x":51,"y":27.4,"n":"Vizzklick","e":1}],"cats":["tailoring"]},"5802":{"id":5802,"t":"Fire Plume Forged","lv":57,"min":55,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Skeleton Key Mold and 2 Thorium Bars to the top of Fire Plume Ridge in Un'Goro Crater. Use the Skeleton Key Mold by the lava lake to forge the Unfinished Skeleton Key.\nBring the Unfinished Skeleton Key to Apothecary Dithers at the Bulwark, Western Plaguelands.\nUnfinished Skeleton Key\nProvided: Skeleton Key Mold","desc":"You need two bars of thorium and a powerfully hot heat source to forge the key stem. You're on your own for the thorium, but I can help with the heat.\nTo our west in Un'Goro Crater is Fire Plume Ridge - a simmering volcano. The lava lake up top is hot enough to fuse thorium and bone together. Your gold has bought you a mold that simply requires you to dip it in the lake up top; the lava will take care of the rest.\nThat's it on my end. To finish your key, you'll need to talk to Dithers again.","rew":"Experience: 4,500","back":"Do you have the stem of the skeletal key finished? I'm truly sorry you had to bear the brunt of the fee to purchase the mold, but we must all do our part to counter the Scourge. Once you hand me the unfinished key, you'll be ready for the final item needed to complete its construction.\nIt won't be easy at all, but the work you've done to date in preparing for an assault on Andorhal will now start to pay for itself. You'll see.","done":"We've got quite the costly skeleton key there, don't we ‹name›? Still, it remains unfinished; the time has now come to put some focus behind our creation. To that end, you're going to have to face the ultimate foe we've been working towards facing in Andorhal... the being that runs the show within the ruined city walls.\nI'm speaking of Araj the Summoner - a lich, and one of the most powerful beings the Scourge calls as its own.\nTanaris Tirisfal Glades Un'Goro Crater","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":51.5,"y":28.8,"n":"Krinkle Goodsteel","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":83.3,"y":69.2,"n":"Apothecary Dithers","e":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"8922":{"id":8922,"t":"A Supernatural Device","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Sealed Blood Container to Mux Manascrambler inside Gadgetzan in Tanaris.\nSealed Blood Container\nProvided: Sealed Blood Container","desc":"I must find a way to speak with Anthion Harmon... or more specifically, his ghost!\nI know of an engineer with a queer interest in the supernatural. He claims he can build a machine that allows him to speak with the dead!\nThe blood you collected was intended for him; travel to Gadgetzan and bring it to him as payment for his services!","rew":"Experience: 6,600","back":"You've something for me?","done":"Excellent! Just as I was running low!\nYou say Deliana sent you?\nDun Morogh Tanaris","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58.1,"y":29.5,"n":"Deliana","s":1},{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.5,"y":27.2,"n":"Mux Manascrambler","e":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"922":{"id":922,"t":"Rellian Greenspyre","lv":7,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a Timberling Seed to Rellian Greenspyre in Darnassus.\nTimberling Seed Elder Timberling , Timberling 37 % , Oakenscowl 20 % , Timberling Mire Beast 20 % and 2 more\nProvided: Timberling Seed","desc":"‹name›, can you take one of the seeds you brought me to my friend, Rellian Greenspyre? He is a druid in Darnassus, and when last we spoke he revealed his interest in my work with the Timberlings. He had some ideas himself, and he will appreciate a specimen seed to work with.\nThank you, ‹name›. You have been a great help to me. I hope that, some day, you will see the fruit of my labors.\nYou will usually find Rellian walking the pathways of the Cenarion Enclave in Darnassus.","rew":"Experience: 320\n+50 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Hello...\nAnd how may I help you?","done":"Ah, a timberling seed? I wanted to try growing one of these to help Denalan with his studies.\nBut I'm afraid I've discovered that a corruption has grown in many of the timberlings, and seeds from such creatures carry their parent's taint. They are beyond my talents to repair.\nDenalan is very skilled with things that grow. He may find a cure for future timberlings. He may be their only hope.\nTeldrassil Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":60.9,"y":68.5,"n":"Denalan","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":38.2,"y":21.6,"n":"Rellian Greenspyre","e":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"6362":{"id":6362,"t":"Ride to Thunder Bluff","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Buy a wind rider to Thunder Bluff from the wind rider master Devrak, then bring the Bundle of Hides to Ahanu in Thunder Bluff.\nBundle of Hides\nProvided: Bundle of Hides","desc":"For a small fee, I will give you a wind rider to Thunder Bluff. There's no faster way to the city!\nIf that is acceptable, speak to me again when you are ready to go.\nIf you're taking those hides to Ahanu, then I think he's at Hewa's Armory, at the base of the wind rider tower in Thunder Bluff. And that's right where you'll land!","rew":"Money: 1 75 0 gold, 1 silver, 75 copper Experience: 420\n+50 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"There is dust on your shoulders that must be from the Barrens. You have spoken with my friend Jahan?","done":"Ah, a new bundle of hides. I will get to work on these immediately!\nThank you, brother. You have done me a great service. Here are some coins to pay for your time and travel costs.\nThe Barrens Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":51.5,"y":30.3,"n":"Devrak","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":45.8,"y":55.8,"n":"Ahanu","e":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"5482":{"id":5482,"t":"Doom Weed","lv":6,"min":5,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect 10 Doom Weed and deliver them back to Junior Apothecary Holland.\n10 Doom Weed Doom Weed","desc":"So you can see the predicament that I'm in, ‹name›. That thing is out there collecting the wrong weeds! I'll make it worth your while to gather what I need. Bring back to me enough doom weed and I'll give you a suitable reward.\nIt is my understanding that they like to plague the flora near the mass gravesite, to the north of the Brill graveyard. Hurry and be mindful of the gnolls in the area.","rew":"Money: 1 25 0 gold, 1 silver, 25 copper Experience: 550\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"This had better be good. I trust you have all of the doom weed that I require?","done":"Ah, my doom weed. Excellent!\n<Junior Apothecary Holland rubs his hands together greedily.>\nThese will come in quite handy. You've done me, uh, the Lady, a fine service today ‹name›. As promised here is the reward that you deserve.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":57.4,"y":48.8,"n":"Junior Apothecary Holland","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"362":{"id":362,"t":"The Haunted Mills","lv":10,"min":7,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Slay Devlin Agamand, and bring Devlin's Remains to Coleman Farthing in Brill.\nDevlin's Remains Devlin Agamand","desc":"Devlin Agamand was the younger of two sons in the Agamand family, and in life the two could not be more different. Thurman was tall and gentle while his younger brother was weak and sharp tongued.\nWhen Agamand Mills fell to the Plague, I was not surprised to hear that Devlin was quick to succumb. His mad chattering can still be heard near the road leading to the Agamand Mills.\nI'm collecting the remains of the Agamands, and I want poor Devlin. Find him, destroy him, and bring me his bones.","rew":"Experience: 420\n+50 reputation with Undercity","back":"Did you find Devlin?","done":"Thank you. Devlin's bones will rest nicely on my mantle.\nIf my cold heart can find warmth, it is in knowing that the Agamands are destroyed. They failed me and my family when the Plague came - now I swear I will smash their remains under my heel!","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.7,"y":52.3,"n":"Coleman Farthing","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"2202":{"id":2202,"t":"Uldaman Reagent Run","lv":42,"min":36,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 12 Magenta Fungus Caps to Jarkal Mossmeld in Kargath.\n12 Magenta Fungus Cap Magenta Cap Clusters , Magenta Cap Clusters","desc":"I've heard about a newly discovered plant called the magenta fungus caps. They grow in clusters at the Uldaman dig site and can be found in the early tunnels and deep within the less-explored areas. I want to study their potential use in alchemy, and that's where you come in.\nFind the magenta cap clusters and bring me a dozen caps. Be warned, the clusters may spew out poison spores if jostled.\nDo this for me, and I'll whip up a batch of one of my famous restorative elixirs for you!","rew":"You will receive:\n5 Restorative Potion\nMoney: 55 0 gold, 55 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,450\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Have you obtained the magenta fungus caps I need for my alchemical work? No caps - no reward!","done":"Well done ‹name›, you've proven your worth once again! The caps will be an interesting study, you betcha.\nAnd now, as promised, enjoy a taste of one of my more potent restorative brews from my personal stock...\nIf you are a skilled alchemist, then perhaps we might have some additional business to conduct. Regardless, I thank you for your assistance!","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":2.4,"y":46.1,"n":"Jarkal Mossmeld","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["uldaman"]},"3882":{"id":3882,"t":"Roll the Bones","lv":51,"min":49,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 8 Dinosaur Bones to Spark Nilminer in Un'Goro Crater.\n8 Dinosaur Bone Dinosaur Bone , Stegodon 28 % , Plated Stegodon 28 % , Spiked Stegodon 28 % and 4 more","desc":"You'd think that being chief digger for Marshal Expeditions means I like digging. There might be worse things to do in this world... but none really leap to mind.\nWe were supposed to be digging in Terror Run - FANTASTIC name by the way - for dead stegodons and diemetradons. Well, there are plenty of live ones there too! Wil and Hol are still all about studying this death trap, so we need those dinosaur bones. Between you and me though, bringing some from live ones will work out just as well.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nArchaeologist's Quarry Boots Excavator's Utility Belt\nExperience: 4,900","back":"Think whatever you want of me, but they're not going to care if the bones they get to research are from ones from ancient stegodons and diemetradons or the ones that almost devoured us wholesale when we were trying to set up our camps. I'll just be happy if we get out of here alive...","done":"Excellent, these should do the trick. And now, if you'll permit me...\nTHANKS FOR DIGGING ALL OF THESE BONES OUT OF THE GROUND FOR US AND NOT HURTING THE NATIVE BEASTS IN ANY WAY.\nWhether you really did or didn't, I don't want to know. Let's keep it that way, shall we? Here - maybe this will keep your lips shut on the whole thing. Anything to get out of here alive, I say!","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":43.5,"y":7.4,"n":"Spark Nilminer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"3962":{"id":3962,"t":"It's Dangerous to Go Alone","lv":56,"min":47,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Fire Plume Ridge, south of Marshal's Refuge.\nFind Blazerunner and use the totem to remove his protective aura. Once he has been defeated, acquire the Golden Flame from the cave.\nGolden Flame Ornate Chest\nSilver Totem of Aquementas\nBlazerunner slain\nProvided: Silver Totem of Aquementas","desc":"‹name›, I finally remember now... I did come here to fight Blazerunner. I was on a journey, and this was to be the last step.\nBut I am no longer the hero... You are. All that you have done -- you must finish this now, not me.\nBlazerunner guards an artifact called the Golden Flame. It provides power more vast than anything else I have ever known, and it is dangerous in the hands of one with an evil heart.\nYou will want to bring others with you -- it's dangerous to go alone. Take this as my advice.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nLinken's Sword of Mastery Spirit of Aquementas\nYou will also receive:\nLinken's Boomerang\nExperience: 7,300","back":"Blazerunner is almost invincible behind the aura he has created by using the Golden Flame. Only you have the power to remove it with the Silver Totem of Aquementas.","done":"Thank you, ‹name›.\nThe Golden Flame will now be returned back to my homeland, where it may be protected, never again to be used for evil.\nSince you did so much for me, I'd like you to have this. Without you, I'd still have no idea who I am!","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":44.7,"y":8.1,"n":"Linken","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"1802":{"id":1802,"t":"Tome of the Cabal","lv":30,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Retrieve the Moldy Tome and Tattered Manuscript for Krom Stoutarm in Ironforge.\nMoldy Tome Tome of the Cabal\nTattered Manuscript Damaged Chest","desc":"It was lost, but there's some idea as to where it might be found.\nThere was only one copy ever made and it was vandalized at some point, a large portion of it ripped from the binding. Rumor has it that it somehow passed into the hands of the centaur of Thousand Needles.\nThe rest was lost off the coast west of Southshore, where it was to be transported to Menethil Harbor by boat. It never arrived.\nIn exchange for this knowledge, all I ask is that if you find it, bring it to me to see.","rew":"Experience: 2,450","back":"Did the rumors prove true, ‹name›?","done":"Fantastic! Now I may join the ranks of the few that have spied its contents.\nI can't wait to further peruse this text. This is a great day, ‹name›! If you will just allow me to glance at it before you leave. I'm sure that Strahad will be willing to send me a copy.\nDun Morogh Hillsbrad Foothills The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":63,"y":22.6,"n":"Krom Stoutarm","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"7562":{"id":7562,"t":"Mor'zul Bloodbringer","lv":58,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Mor'zul Bloodbringer in the Burning Steppes.","desc":"‹name›, your delvings into the dark arts are deep. Your mastery over otherworldly denizens has grown so strong... perhaps you are ready to bind to you one of the infamous dreadsteeds.\nThe ritual to summon the beast from its home requires great power and resources, but if you desire to dominate that epic mount, then speak with Mor'zul Bloodbringer. He is camped near the Altar of Storms in the Burning Steppes.\nGo, ‹name›. This quest will be perilous, but a Warlock of your stature does not shy from danger!","rew":"Experience: 625","done":"Greetings, ‹name›, and welcome. Are you here to study near the Altar of Storms as I am, perhaps to harness its energy for some hidden purpose...\nOr... are you here to speak with me? Yes, I believe you are.\nYou want to master a dreadsteed? Such is no easy task. It will cost you no small amounts of blood, sweat... and of course gold. But a dreadsteed of Xoroth is a prize well worth winning so if interested, listen on...\nStormwind City Orgrimmar Dun Morogh Swamp of Sorrows Burning Steppes","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":39.5,"y":84.5,"n":"Spackle Thornberry","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":47.5,"y":46.7,"n":"Kurgul","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":59.5,"y":22.1,"n":"Jubahl Corpseseeker","s":1},{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":48.6,"y":55.3,"n":"Greshka","s":1},{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":12.7,"y":31.6,"n":"Mor'zul Bloodbringer","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"5402":{"id":5402,"t":"Minion's Scourgestones","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"20 Minion's Scourgestone Skeletal Terror 50 % , Slavering Ghoul 50 % , Hungering Wraith 50 % , Foulmane 50 % and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\nArgent Dawn Valor Token\nExperience: 550\n+25 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"A Minion's Scourgestone is the insignia of the Scourge rank and file. These are sometimes found on the weaker of their troops positioned in the Plaguelands, though the term \"weaker\" is certainly to be considered in context. The Scourge, no matter where they are, should never be underestimated.\nThe Argent Dawn currently offers a valor token in exchange for twenty of these insignia - an exchange I'm happy to do, provided you have earned enough scourgestones!","done":"Congratulations, ‹name› - I am pleased to award you with an Argent Dawn valor token!\nThe tokens serve two purposes. One - they can be used to further your standing within the Argent Dawn; to do so may avail you options and rewards that are reserved for our honored and revered allies. Two - they can be given to our quartermasters, along with coin, as payment for some of the Dawn's more prized items.\nWhatever you decide, know that you are earning your commission. Well done!","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":43,"y":83.5,"n":"Argent Officer Pureheart","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"5162":{"id":5162,"t":"Wrath of the Blue Flight","lv":60,"min":57,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 7,050, 0.94 times as much.","obj":"Speak with Jeziba in the Plaguelands. He resides in Andorhal.","desc":"It is the arcane that I control and the arcane which will send you to your next destination.\nWhen you are ready, the journey will begin. To the Plaguelands you will go and to Jeziba you will speak.\nHe is a mortal as wise as the ancients and as patient as the immovable earth. Find him in Andorhal.","rew":"Experience: 6,600","done":"I am Jeziba, known to many as the Sculptor. What I sculpt, however, are not statues, but heroes.\nWinterspring Western Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":54.5,"y":51.2,"n":"Haleh","s":1},{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":39.4,"y":66.8,"n":"Jeziba","e":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"98282":{"id":98282,"t":"Alchemical hazards","lv":22,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect an Unruptured Stalker Gland from Thelgen Rock for Caitlin Grassman in Menethil Harbor.\nUnruptured Stalker Gland","desc":"Certain alchemical recipes require ingredients sourced from, well, very dangerous places. And those are often just the base herbs! The other ingredients are even worse!\nI need to make more antivenom before I can leave again. I swear everything in this marsh is venomous. It's like it runs through the land itself!\nCan you help me? I'll need a venom gland from the spiders in Thelgen Rock to the far southeast. But it has to be unruptured, or too much venom will spill out before you can get here. Sorry!","rew":"You will receive:\n5 Strong Anti-Venom\nExperience: 1,750","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":11.8,"y":58.6,"n":"Caitlin Grassman","s":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"4842":{"id":4842,"t":"Strange Sources","lv":56,"min":51,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Follow Donova Snowden's instructions, then report back.\nFind the place the quest sends you to.","desc":"To tell you the truth, although there are no volcanoes here in Winterspring, I believe that there are far more threatening reasons for these hot springs...\nWell, I think you'll want to see it for yourself. You'll need to travel the length of Winterspring, and head to the very south. When the air becomes thick and muggy, and the sky turns dark, you'll have found what I believe to be the source of the hot springs.\nHave a look. I'm sure you'll have many questions when you return.","rew":"You will receive:\nDeep River Cloak\nExperience: 5,800\n+100 reputation with Everlook","back":"The water in the springs seems to have some very odd properties... I am still unsure of what it means...","done":"Yes, the demons there in Darkwhisper Gorge; I believe it is their presence that is affecting the land in this way. I am going to continue observing the hot springs here and see if I learn anything more.\nI'd wait until you are a bit stronger if you have plans of heading farther into Darkwhisper Gorge.","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":31.3,"y":45.2,"n":"Donova Snowden","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"5082":{"id":5082,"t":"Threat of the Winterfall","lv":56,"min":52,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Donova Snowden in Winterspring wants you to kill 8 Winterfall Pathfinders, 8 Winterfall Den Watchers, and 8 Winterfall Totemics.\nWinterfall Pathfinder slain : 0/ 8\nWinterfall Den Watcher slain : 0/ 8\nWinterfall Totemic slain : 0/ 8","desc":"I came to Winterspring to investigate the Frostfire Hot Springs. I've noticed that the water seems to have ...strange qualities. I haven't yet been able to discover the source, and to tell you the truth, I've had some difficulty lately, due to the Winterfall furbolg.\nThey seem to be drawn to the springs, just as I am. They have become extremely protective of the water, and won't let me come near the two larger springs to the north of here.\nI'd like to continue my studies, so won't you help me?","rew":"Money: 85 0 gold, 85 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,800\n+100 reputation with Everlook","back":"I appreciate your help!","done":"Thanks so much, ‹name›! Now I can get back to work here.\nDid you find anything of interest at the Winterfall camp?","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":31.3,"y":45.2,"n":"Donova Snowden","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"92682":{"id":92682,"t":"Make yourself useful","lv":9,"min":5,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Gather 10 Ripe Stormapples and slay 5 Hungry Bandits at the Windfield Orchard.\n10 Ripe Stormapple\nHungry Bandit slain : 0/ 5","desc":"Oh, so you've got more courage than sense, then? Fine, I won't argue.\nFerauu and his goons aren't due to pick up their take of the harvest just yet, so I'm going to put you to work for your meals until they arrive.\nHead outside and gather today's batch of stormapples for me. Oh, and the bandits lurking around the stormapple trees... They think they are sneaky. They aren't. Kill them for me.\nLet's see what you've got in a fight.","rew":"You will receive:\n5 Red Delicious Stormapple\nExperience: 775","back":"These bandits are more likely to double cross and steal from each other than they are to steal from normal folks. I bet if Ferauu knew some of his people went rogue and came here early to tamper with the harvest, he'd kill them himself.","done":"I watched you take down those bandits from the window. Not bad.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":46.6,"y":81.8,"n":"Aamelia Windfield","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"8042":{"id":8042,"t":"Strength of Mount Mugamba","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60.","obj":"Strength of Mugamba","rew":"You will receive:\nStrength of Mugamba\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"It is good to see you in good health, ‹name›. The glorious battles you have undertaken affect all life on this planet. Hakkar must never leave the confines of Zul'Gurub as the world will surely collapse beneath his immense hunger.\nGive me your talisman and I shall amplify its strength. Use the Strength of Mugamba to punish our enemies!","done":"Our paths will cross again, ‹class›.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":14.4,"n":"Jin'rokh the Breaker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zulgurub"]}});